WEBVTT

1
00:00:46,820 --> 00:00:51,030
Within five days, Muzan will come.

2
00:00:57,500 --> 00:01:00,240
Use me as bait

3
00:01:00,980 --> 00:01:03,750
and take Muzan's head for me.

4
00:01:07,510 --> 00:01:11,380
Why do you think he will come?

5
00:01:14,390 --> 00:01:19,640
It is just intuition. No reason.

6
00:01:20,260 --> 00:01:23,729
The other children

7
00:01:23,730 --> 00:01:30,650
would never agree
to use me as bait.

8
00:01:31,450 --> 00:01:35,780
I can only entrust this to you, Gyomei.

9
00:01:38,040 --> 00:01:41,370
He does not die
even if you cut off his head.

10
00:01:43,620 --> 00:01:50,550
I suppose the only thing that
can destroy Muzan is sunlight.

11
00:01:51,630 --> 00:01:54,549
If cutting off his head

12
00:01:54,550 --> 00:01:57,099
does not kill him,

13
00:01:57,100 --> 00:02:00,980
your fight will be a battle
of endurance until sunrise.

14
00:02:02,480 --> 00:02:03,640
Understood.

15
00:02:05,150 --> 00:02:08,020
If that is your wish, Master.

16
00:02:11,530 --> 00:02:13,070
Thank you.

17
00:02:18,790 --> 00:02:26,419
I just hope that no more of

18
00:02:26,420 --> 00:02:29,360
my precious children have to die.

19
00:02:47,520 --> 00:02:51,190
Do you think you've got me cornered?

20
00:02:52,940 --> 00:02:56,699
You are all now going to Hell!

21
00:02:56,700 --> 00:02:58,779
You demon hunters are an eyesore!

22
00:02:58,780 --> 00:03:01,950
Tonight, I'm going to slaughter
every last one of you!

23
00:03:06,540 --> 00:03:09,170
You're the one who's going to Hell, Muzan!

24
00:03:09,660 --> 00:03:11,550
I won't let you escape!

25
00:03:12,170 --> 00:03:16,509
Do it if you can!

26
00:03:16,510 --> 00:03:19,050
Tanjiro Kamado!

27
00:03:21,350 --> 00:03:23,310
I'll defeat you for sure!

28
00:03:24,850 --> 00:03:26,979
Muzan Kibutsuji!

29
00:03:26,980 --> 00:03:32,280
DEMON SLAYER: KIMETSU NO YAIBA
INFINITY CASTLE - PART I: AKAZA RETURNS

30
00:03:38,820 --> 00:03:40,410
What is this place?

31
00:03:41,450 --> 00:03:43,410
Up, down, left, right,
it's all a total mess.

32
00:03:44,620 --> 00:03:48,330
Is it created by
the enemy's Blood Demon Art?

33
00:03:50,880 --> 00:03:53,379
I don't know what is going on exactly,

34
00:03:53,380 --> 00:03:55,880
but I know Miss Tamayo
is holding off Muzan.

35
00:03:57,260 --> 00:04:00,850
However, I don't know
how long she can hold.

36
00:04:03,310 --> 00:04:05,220
Calm down, Kanroji!

37
00:04:05,730 --> 00:04:07,349
Okay!

38
00:04:07,350 --> 00:04:08,690
Stay close to me.

39
00:05:03,620 --> 00:05:07,200
I need to get to Muzan as soon
as possible and take him out.

40
00:05:07,950 --> 00:05:09,620
As soon as possible!

41
00:05:17,800 --> 00:05:18,920
I see the bottom.

42
00:05:19,380 --> 00:05:21,429
If I hit the bottom, I'll die.

43
00:05:21,430 --> 00:05:23,639
I have to use a technique
to change my trajectory

44
00:05:23,640 --> 00:05:25,850
and grab onto the building somewhere.

45
00:05:29,350 --> 00:05:30,729
I'm out of position.

46
00:05:30,730 --> 00:05:33,350
I can't take a stance
because of the fall.

47
00:06:22,650 --> 00:06:24,030
Are you all right?

48
00:06:25,910 --> 00:06:28,490
Yes! Thank you!

49
00:06:30,080 --> 00:06:31,140
You saved—

50
00:06:33,370 --> 00:06:36,039
Water Breathing, First Form:

51
00:06:36,040 --> 00:06:37,500
Water Surface Slash!

52
00:06:39,920 --> 00:06:41,380
Tanjiro!

53
00:07:03,150 --> 00:07:04,819
Water Breathing...

54
00:07:04,820 --> 00:07:06,159
Sixth Form:

55
00:07:06,160 --> 00:07:07,820
Third Form:

56
00:07:09,570 --> 00:07:11,039
Whirlpool!

57
00:07:11,040 --> 00:07:12,540
Flowing Dance!

58
00:07:20,590 --> 00:07:22,610
Giyu is incredible.

59
00:07:23,130 --> 00:07:26,429
From my slight movement, he grasped
what technique I was going to use,

60
00:07:26,430 --> 00:07:30,430
then he used one himself,
and made sure we wouldn't clash.

61
00:07:31,010 --> 00:07:32,770
This person is insane.

62
00:07:33,350 --> 00:07:35,940
I can't even read his face.

63
00:07:38,560 --> 00:07:42,399
This is probably the demon hideout
that Shinazugawa and Iguro

64
00:07:42,400 --> 00:07:44,280
were talking about.

65
00:07:47,360 --> 00:07:48,779
If that's the case,

66
00:07:48,780 --> 00:07:51,909
then Kibutsuji's goal
in gathering us here is

67
00:07:51,910 --> 00:07:54,620
to wipe out the Corps,
including the Hashiras.

68
00:07:56,160 --> 00:08:00,080
From this point on,
we'll have to be even more cautious.

69
00:08:00,960 --> 00:08:01,920
Yes.

70
00:08:03,460 --> 00:08:04,799
STEP STEP
Let's go!

71
00:08:04,800 --> 00:08:05,659
STEP STEP
Yes!

72
00:08:05,660 --> 00:08:06,630
STEP STEP

73
00:08:28,280 --> 00:08:31,120
Serpent Breathing, Fifth Form:

74
00:08:38,120 --> 00:08:39,890
Slithering Serpent.

75
00:08:42,790 --> 00:08:46,760
Don't get close to Kanroji, you trash.

76
00:08:48,340 --> 00:08:50,890
Iguro! You're wonderful!

77
00:08:51,970 --> 00:08:52,799
Are you hurt?

78
00:08:52,800 --> 00:08:53,849
No!

79
00:08:53,850 --> 00:08:54,679
Let's go.

80
00:08:54,680 --> 00:08:55,810
Okay!

81
00:09:16,620 --> 00:09:17,580
Tokito!

82
00:09:24,750 --> 00:09:27,169
What an incredible number of demons.

83
00:09:27,170 --> 00:09:30,589
It seems they have been imbued
with the same strength as a Lower Rank.

84
00:09:30,590 --> 00:09:34,260
They are trying to wear us down.

85
00:09:39,680 --> 00:09:41,600
What about Master?

86
00:09:42,020 --> 00:09:44,230
He has passed away.

87
00:09:45,520 --> 00:09:47,780
It was a dignified end.

88
00:09:49,240 --> 00:09:54,620
I don't think he would make
the mistake of letting the demon find him.

89
00:09:55,070 --> 00:09:56,780
Did he become bait himself?

90
00:09:57,740 --> 00:10:01,960
Yes. He knew he didn't
have much time to live.

91
00:10:08,750 --> 00:10:10,340
Master...

92
00:10:17,140 --> 00:10:21,229
He stayed with me the whole time

93
00:10:21,230 --> 00:10:24,229
when I was on the verge of death

94
00:10:24,230 --> 00:10:26,520
after being attacked by a demon.

95
00:10:28,830 --> 00:10:33,490
He did the same for other members
in their rough moments.

96
00:10:35,610 --> 00:10:37,410
Like a father would.

97
00:10:39,370 --> 00:10:41,540
Yeah, I know.

98
00:10:42,430 --> 00:10:44,749
Not just my big brother,

99
00:10:44,750 --> 00:10:47,460
Muzan even killed our father figure.

100
00:10:48,130 --> 00:10:50,959
Muzan... He...

101
00:10:50,960 --> 00:10:53,589
I'll make him suffer.

102
00:10:53,590 --> 00:10:55,710
I'll show him Hell.

103
00:10:56,720 --> 00:10:58,390
Don't worry.

104
00:11:02,810 --> 00:11:05,850
We all feel the same.

105
00:11:12,740 --> 00:11:14,450
Master...

106
00:11:16,700 --> 00:11:18,490
I couldn't protect him.

107
00:11:34,130 --> 00:11:37,220
You vermin crawling out
one after another.

108
00:11:40,430 --> 00:11:42,719
Bring it on!

109
00:11:42,720 --> 00:11:45,180
I'll murder you all!

110
00:11:54,280 --> 00:11:57,610
Pig assault!

111
00:12:00,450 --> 00:12:02,869
I got dropped again!

112
00:12:02,870 --> 00:12:04,079
Take this!

113
00:12:04,080 --> 00:12:07,459
Somehow I ended up
in some totally random place,

114
00:12:07,460 --> 00:12:09,709
but with all these demons
popping out like crazy,

115
00:12:09,710 --> 00:12:14,550
it's a perfect chance
to put my training to the test!

116
00:12:24,600 --> 00:12:26,429
What the heck is this place?

117
00:12:26,430 --> 00:12:27,729
Is this the demon stronghold?

118
00:12:27,730 --> 00:12:29,140
Where is everyone?

119
00:12:29,810 --> 00:12:30,980
Big Bro...

120
00:12:32,320 --> 00:12:34,360
I hope he's okay.

121
00:12:39,150 --> 00:12:40,990
I heard something.

122
00:12:41,570 --> 00:12:43,910
He may be close.

123
00:12:49,460 --> 00:12:51,500
I won't forgive him.

124
00:12:52,750 --> 00:12:56,420
I'll never forgive that bastard.

125
00:13:20,740 --> 00:13:22,510
I smell blood.

126
00:13:31,460 --> 00:13:33,130
What is this place?

127
00:13:52,450 --> 00:13:54,610
My, someone came?

128
00:13:55,330 --> 00:13:57,940
Wow! A girl!

129
00:13:58,610 --> 00:14:02,200
You look young and tasty.

130
00:14:02,820 --> 00:14:06,700
I'll thank Nakime later.

131
00:14:21,840 --> 00:14:27,180
Shinobu... Quit the Demon Slayer Corps.

132
00:14:28,680 --> 00:14:31,909
You're doing your best.

133
00:14:31,910 --> 00:14:34,900
I know you're doing your best,

134
00:14:35,650 --> 00:14:38,110
but I think you...

135
00:14:43,740 --> 00:14:47,740
I want you to be a normal girl
and be happy...

136
00:14:48,320 --> 00:14:51,520
And live until you become old.

137
00:14:53,460 --> 00:14:56,289
You've done enough.

138
00:14:56,290 --> 00:14:59,209
No! I'll never quit!

139
00:14:59,210 --> 00:15:02,089
I'll avenge you!

140
00:15:02,090 --> 00:15:04,469
Tell me! What kind of demon was it?

141
00:15:04,470 --> 00:15:06,430
Who got you?!

142
00:15:07,090 --> 00:15:09,259
Big Sis Kanae, tell me!

143
00:15:09,260 --> 00:15:10,750
Please!

144
00:15:11,330 --> 00:15:12,599
After all of this,

145
00:15:12,600 --> 00:15:15,599
there's no way I can live
a normal life!

146
00:15:15,600 --> 00:15:17,310
Big Sis!

147
00:15:21,940 --> 00:15:26,320
It was a demon that looked like
it was drenched in blood over his head.

148
00:15:28,130 --> 00:15:31,579
Heya there. Nice to meet you.

149
00:15:31,580 --> 00:15:34,289
My name is Doma.

150
00:15:34,290 --> 00:15:37,420
What a beautiful night.

151
00:15:38,960 --> 00:15:41,790
Smiling innocently, without a care.

152
00:15:42,590 --> 00:15:45,900
Speaking gently and kindly.

153
00:15:47,300 --> 00:15:50,759
He... Help...

154
00:15:50,760 --> 00:15:51,890
Help me!

155
00:15:53,930 --> 00:15:55,980
I'm talking to her.

156
00:16:00,810 --> 00:16:02,450
Are you all right?

157
00:16:04,070 --> 00:16:05,569
You're fast.

158
00:16:05,570 --> 00:16:07,360
Are you a Hashira?

159
00:16:15,980 --> 00:16:19,999
Don't mind it.
Just leave her there.

160
00:16:20,000 --> 00:16:22,250
I'll eat her properly later.

161
00:16:25,550 --> 00:16:32,470
The weapon he uses
is a pair of sharp fans.

162
00:16:34,930 --> 00:16:39,519
I am the founder
of the Eternal Paradise Faith.

163
00:16:39,520 --> 00:16:43,519
It's my duty to find happiness
together with my followers.

164
00:16:43,520 --> 00:16:46,570
I'll devour that girl later,
without leaving a single trace.

165
00:16:47,690 --> 00:16:51,740
So he is the demon
who killed my sister.

166
00:16:53,280 --> 00:16:55,369
Finding happiness together?

167
00:16:55,370 --> 00:16:57,119
Ridiculous!

168
00:16:57,120 --> 00:17:00,829
She didn't want it
and begged for help.

169
00:17:00,830 --> 00:17:02,980
That's why I helped her.

170
00:17:03,500 --> 00:17:08,299
Now she's no longer in pain, suffering,

171
00:17:08,300 --> 00:17:10,259
or afraid.

172
00:17:10,260 --> 00:17:13,469
Everyone fears death,

173
00:17:13,470 --> 00:17:16,349
which is why I eat them.

174
00:17:16,350 --> 00:17:20,810
So they'll live on with me.
Forever inside me.

175
00:17:21,680 --> 00:17:26,149
I completely accept the feelings,
the blood, and the flesh of my believers,

176
00:17:26,150 --> 00:17:28,899
and through that,
I offer them salvation

177
00:17:28,900 --> 00:17:31,330
and guide them to a higher place.

178
00:17:31,910 --> 00:17:34,879
You are insane.

179
00:17:34,880 --> 00:17:37,289
Is your head all right?

180
00:17:37,290 --> 00:17:39,410
You really make me sick.

181
00:17:41,920 --> 00:17:45,749
It's our first meeting,
but you're so hostile.

182
00:17:45,750 --> 00:17:47,419
I see.

183
00:17:47,420 --> 00:17:49,549
Poor you.

184
00:17:49,550 --> 00:17:52,429
You must have experienced
something painful.

185
00:17:52,430 --> 00:17:55,420
I'll listen to you. You can tell me.

186
00:17:56,720 --> 00:18:00,019
Of course it's painful!

187
00:18:00,020 --> 00:18:03,229
It was you who killed my sister!

188
00:18:03,230 --> 00:18:06,230
Does this haori ring a bell?

189
00:18:20,830 --> 00:18:24,119
Was it the Flower Breathing girl?

190
00:18:24,120 --> 00:18:27,519
She was kind and cute.

191
00:18:27,520 --> 00:18:30,509
I couldn't devour her
because the sun came up.

192
00:18:30,510 --> 00:18:31,969
I remember.

193
00:18:31,970 --> 00:18:34,380
I really wanted to eat her.

194
00:18:36,470 --> 00:18:39,679
Insect Breathing, Dance of the Bee Sting:

195
00:18:39,680 --> 00:18:41,140
True Flutter.

196
00:18:41,850 --> 00:18:43,689
What an amazing thrust.

197
00:18:43,690 --> 00:18:45,600
I couldn't stop it with my hand.

198
00:18:47,610 --> 00:18:49,010
Blood Demon Art:

199
00:18:50,440 --> 00:18:53,070
Frozen Lotus.

200
00:18:53,650 --> 00:18:54,609
It's cold!

201
00:18:54,610 --> 00:18:57,490
Air so frigid,
it's tearing through my lungs!

202
00:18:59,620 --> 00:19:01,830
You're fast. So fast.

203
00:19:02,370 --> 00:19:04,539
But what a shame.

204
00:19:04,540 --> 00:19:07,710
Thrust techniques
can't kill demons.

205
00:19:10,920 --> 00:19:12,849
Aim my neck.

206
00:19:12,850 --> 00:19:15,180
You must sever my head.

207
00:19:17,760 --> 00:19:20,639
Sure, a thrust can't kill you.

208
00:19:20,640 --> 00:19:22,270
What about poison?

209
00:19:26,770 --> 00:19:30,980
I'll soon know if this poison
works on an Upper Rank or not.

210
00:19:32,280 --> 00:19:35,090
Big Sis, please...

211
00:19:35,680 --> 00:19:36,990
Big Sis!

212
00:19:39,070 --> 00:19:40,989
This poison...

213
00:19:40,990 --> 00:19:46,420
is stronger than the one you used
on Rui's Mountain.

214
00:19:47,440 --> 00:19:50,539
I knew it, they were sharing information.

215
00:19:50,540 --> 00:19:52,589
Poison is a double-edged sword.

216
00:19:52,590 --> 00:20:00,100
My Lord said you adjust the compound
for each individual demon.

217
00:20:07,230 --> 00:20:13,319
Oh, look. It seems like I managed to
break down the poison.

218
00:20:13,320 --> 00:20:14,859
Sorry about that.

219
00:20:14,860 --> 00:20:18,110
You went to the trouble of using it on me.

220
00:20:19,110 --> 00:20:24,370
That sword makes a unique sound
when you sheath it.

221
00:20:24,870 --> 00:20:28,500
Is that when you adjust the compound?

222
00:20:29,830 --> 00:20:31,250
This is fun!

223
00:20:31,960 --> 00:20:36,879
Getting poisoned is interesting!
I might get addicted to it!

224
00:20:36,880 --> 00:20:39,100
Do you think the next compound will work?

225
00:20:39,650 --> 00:20:41,470
Give it a try!

226
00:20:47,770 --> 00:20:49,350
Sure.

227
00:20:50,020 --> 00:20:51,649
I'll try it again.

228
00:20:51,650 --> 00:20:52,980
After all...

229
00:20:56,320 --> 00:20:59,140
I've anticipated everything so far.

230
00:21:01,160 --> 00:21:03,119
Are you done adjusting the compound?

231
00:21:03,120 --> 00:21:05,330
Whenever you're ready.

232
00:21:09,290 --> 00:21:12,170
I did say to give it a try,

233
00:21:13,790 --> 00:21:16,740
but using the same technique
feels kind of dull.

234
00:21:31,920 --> 00:21:35,610
Huh? It's slower than before.

235
00:21:36,100 --> 00:21:37,229
At this rate—

236
00:21:37,230 --> 00:21:40,239
Insect Breathing, Dance of the Horsefly:

237
00:21:40,240 --> 00:21:42,070
Enticing Slash!

238
00:21:50,290 --> 00:21:53,379
Wow, I got hit.

239
00:21:53,380 --> 00:21:56,169
You managed to deflect my attack.

240
00:21:56,170 --> 00:21:59,379
That's amazing!
I'm really impressed.

241
00:21:59,380 --> 00:22:02,379
It's the fruit of your tearful hard work.

242
00:22:02,380 --> 00:22:04,679
Keep it coming.

243
00:22:04,680 --> 00:22:08,639
Go ahead and launch your next attack
before the poison breaks down.

244
00:22:08,640 --> 00:22:10,979
I can't help but want to cheer on

245
00:22:10,980 --> 00:22:13,140
someone who's doing their best.

246
00:22:19,340 --> 00:22:21,780
That's it! Keep it up!

247
00:22:24,660 --> 00:22:28,950
Since I was a kid,
I have been kind and clever.

248
00:22:29,700 --> 00:22:35,249
I always helped people in need
and made them happy.

249
00:22:35,250 --> 00:22:37,410
Because that was my duty.

250
00:22:38,880 --> 00:22:42,379
There are rainbows in this child's eyes.

251
00:22:42,380 --> 00:22:46,470
Pale gray hair is proof of innocence.

252
00:22:46,930 --> 00:22:49,389
This child is special.

253
00:22:49,390 --> 00:22:52,350
I believe he can even hear
the voices of the gods.

254
00:22:54,020 --> 00:22:57,760
My parents were so hopeless.

255
00:22:58,440 --> 00:22:59,859
If they weren't stupid,

256
00:22:59,860 --> 00:23:03,700
they wouldn't create the ridiculous
Paradise Faith religion.

257
00:23:04,320 --> 00:23:06,819
I felt sorry for them,

258
00:23:06,820 --> 00:23:09,950
so I always played along.

259
00:23:10,990 --> 00:23:13,870
I never once heard the voices of the gods.

260
00:23:14,910 --> 00:23:16,079
At first,

261
00:23:16,080 --> 00:23:18,919
everyone worshipped
and prayed to me.

262
00:23:18,920 --> 00:23:21,060
It left me at a loss.

263
00:23:22,160 --> 00:23:23,879
When adults come to a child crying,

264
00:23:23,880 --> 00:23:28,469
saying they're in pain, it's too hard,
asking what they should do,

265
00:23:28,470 --> 00:23:31,510
I can't help but worry
if they're mentally okay.

266
00:23:32,520 --> 00:23:36,100
After they shared their
yawn-inducing life stories,

267
00:23:36,610 --> 00:23:40,440
they would bow and say they wanted me
to lead them to paradise.

268
00:23:41,520 --> 00:23:43,110
I cried.

269
00:23:44,030 --> 00:23:45,450
How pitiful.

270
00:23:46,180 --> 00:23:48,740
There's no such thing as paradise.

271
00:23:49,620 --> 00:23:53,620
It's just a fairy tale that humans
created with their imaginations.

272
00:23:54,620 --> 00:23:57,040
The gods and Buddhas
don't exist either.

273
00:23:57,670 --> 00:24:03,130
Even though they had been alive for decades,
they couldn't understand something simple.

274
00:24:03,960 --> 00:24:06,170
When you die,
you just become nothing.

275
00:24:06,720 --> 00:24:08,890
You just stop feeling anything.

276
00:24:10,010 --> 00:24:13,469
Your heart stops.
Your brain stops.

277
00:24:13,470 --> 00:24:15,700
You rot and return to the earth.

278
00:24:16,430 --> 00:24:19,650
That is inevitable for every living thing.

279
00:24:21,900 --> 00:24:24,960
They couldn't accept
something so simple.

280
00:24:25,570 --> 00:24:27,760
It must be difficult to be dumb.

281
00:24:28,910 --> 00:24:32,529
I wanted to make the pitiful people happy.

282
00:24:32,530 --> 00:24:34,160
I wanted to help them.

283
00:24:34,990 --> 00:24:39,460
That is why I was born.

284
00:24:47,010 --> 00:24:48,509
It's the fifth.

285
00:24:48,510 --> 00:24:50,089
It was no good either.

286
00:24:50,090 --> 00:24:51,679
Didn't work.

287
00:24:51,680 --> 00:24:54,719
It's getting less and less effective.

288
00:24:54,720 --> 00:24:58,439
How many more times
can you compound the poison?

289
00:24:58,440 --> 00:25:01,269
Are you having trouble breathing?

290
00:25:01,270 --> 00:25:04,230
You're sweating a lot.
Are you all right?

291
00:25:04,820 --> 00:25:08,150
So this is the strength of an Upper Rank.

292
00:25:08,690 --> 00:25:10,740
My poison isn't working at all.

293
00:25:11,530 --> 00:25:14,320
His speed in building resistance
is abnormal.

294
00:25:16,980 --> 00:25:19,410
That's because the alveoli
in your lungs are dying.

295
00:25:21,250 --> 00:25:22,829
It must be hard.

296
00:25:22,830 --> 00:25:26,170
Since you inhaled my Blood Demon Art
a moment ago.

297
00:25:28,300 --> 00:25:33,090
He turned his frozen blood into a mist
and spread it with his fans.

298
00:25:33,720 --> 00:25:37,220
Breathing itself
is becoming dangerous here.

299
00:25:44,690 --> 00:25:48,820
I'll use continuous attacks to inject
a large dose of poison!

300
00:25:49,690 --> 00:25:52,780
Insect Breathing, Dance of the Dragonfly:

301
00:25:59,500 --> 00:26:01,370
Compound Eye Hexagon!

302
00:26:04,170 --> 00:26:07,959
Wow, you're really fast.

303
00:26:07,960 --> 00:26:11,460
Maybe the fastest Hashira
I've met so far.

304
00:26:15,360 --> 00:26:17,720
I got cut?

305
00:26:19,870 --> 00:26:21,099
Instead of using poison,

306
00:26:21,100 --> 00:26:23,809
you should have severed my head.

307
00:26:23,810 --> 00:26:26,360
If you're that fast,
you might've won.

308
00:26:28,270 --> 00:26:29,529
Maybe not.

309
00:26:29,530 --> 00:26:32,320
Because you're small.

310
00:26:35,410 --> 00:26:39,040
Why are my hands so small?

311
00:26:40,450 --> 00:26:43,620
Why didn't I grow taller?

312
00:26:45,500 --> 00:26:49,169
If I had been just a little taller,

313
00:26:49,170 --> 00:26:52,090
could I have taken his head?

314
00:26:53,050 --> 00:26:58,799
If my arms and legs were longer
and had more muscle,

315
00:26:58,800 --> 00:27:00,630
they would have given me
an advantage.

316
00:27:03,230 --> 00:27:08,340
My sister was delicate, even though
she was taller than I was.

317
00:27:10,070 --> 00:27:12,610
I envy Himejima.

318
00:27:13,360 --> 00:27:17,700
Everyone would feel relieved
when he comes to the rescue.

319
00:27:21,580 --> 00:27:27,380
I know what she was going to say.

320
00:27:30,800 --> 00:27:34,839
Huh? So you can't go on, eh?

321
00:27:34,840 --> 00:27:36,470
Fine, then.

322
00:27:39,890 --> 00:27:43,090
"You will probably lose to that demon."

323
00:27:43,740 --> 00:27:47,810
She was going to say that, but stopped.

324
00:27:48,690 --> 00:27:50,360
Pull yourself together.

325
00:27:56,320 --> 00:27:58,410
I won't allow you to cry.

326
00:27:59,490 --> 00:28:01,489
Big Sis...

327
00:28:01,490 --> 00:28:03,089
Stand up.

328
00:28:03,090 --> 00:28:06,079
I can't. I've lost so much blood.

329
00:28:06,080 --> 00:28:09,960
My left lung is punctured
and I can't breathe.

330
00:28:10,590 --> 00:28:12,420
That doesn't matter.

331
00:28:12,920 --> 00:28:14,299
Stand up,

332
00:28:14,300 --> 00:28:16,760
Insect Hashira Shinobu Kocho.

333
00:28:18,930 --> 00:28:21,719
Once you decide to defeat him,
then defeat him.

334
00:28:21,720 --> 00:28:23,940
Once you decide to win, then win.

335
00:28:25,180 --> 00:28:27,630
You must win, whatever the cost.

336
00:28:28,180 --> 00:28:31,860
Didn't you promise me and Kanao?

337
00:28:34,400 --> 00:28:35,860
Kanao...

338
00:28:38,740 --> 00:28:40,489
Sorry, sorry.

339
00:28:40,490 --> 00:28:43,120
You must be suffering
because it wasn't a thorough cut.

340
00:28:47,910 --> 00:28:51,790
I believe you can do this.
So give it your all.

341
00:28:58,680 --> 00:28:59,759
You can stand?

342
00:28:59,760 --> 00:29:02,849
You're standing, oh my.

343
00:29:02,850 --> 00:29:06,350
Are you really a human?

344
00:29:06,850 --> 00:29:11,350
Even though I cut your collarbone,
lung, and ribs...

345
00:29:11,810 --> 00:29:14,069
For your size,

346
00:29:14,070 --> 00:29:18,740
you should've been dead
with that much blood loss.

347
00:29:19,610 --> 00:29:20,949
See?

348
00:29:20,950 --> 00:29:24,079
The blood in your lungs
is making a rattling sound.

349
00:29:24,080 --> 00:29:27,139
The pain must be unimaginable.

350
00:29:27,140 --> 00:29:29,909
I'll swiftly pop off your head right away.

351
00:29:29,910 --> 00:29:31,290
So don't push yourself.

352
00:29:32,080 --> 00:29:35,799
You're beyond saving.
Don't be so stubborn.

353
00:29:35,800 --> 00:29:38,799
If I'm going to aim,
it's got to be his neck.

354
00:29:38,800 --> 00:29:42,180
If I inject poison into his neck,
I have a chance to win!

355
00:29:42,890 --> 00:29:46,560
Insect Breathing, Dance of the Centipede:

356
00:29:48,310 --> 00:29:50,310
Hundred-Legged Zigzag.

357
00:30:13,210 --> 00:30:16,160
The movements are writhing
in all directions.

358
00:30:16,670 --> 00:30:18,960
Her steps are so forceful
they could split a bridge.

359
00:30:21,800 --> 00:30:24,680
She's fast and keeps attacking.

360
00:30:30,890 --> 00:30:31,730
So low.

361
00:30:45,530 --> 00:30:47,730
I once believed that

362
00:30:48,700 --> 00:30:55,500
the road of happiness continued
forever and far away.

363
00:30:59,050 --> 00:31:01,220
When it was destroyed,

364
00:31:01,860 --> 00:31:07,470
I realized that happiness lies
atop a thin sheet of glass.

365
00:31:10,580 --> 00:31:14,810
And just as we were saved,

366
00:31:15,810 --> 00:31:18,439
there is happiness
that hasn't been destroyed.

367
00:31:18,440 --> 00:31:25,230
So I wanted to get stronger
and protect that happiness.

368
00:31:26,830 --> 00:31:30,790
That was our promise.

369
00:31:32,950 --> 00:31:38,750
"Let's defeat as many demons
as possible together."

370
00:31:41,670 --> 00:31:47,090
We won't let anyone else experience
what we went through.

371
00:31:55,820 --> 00:31:57,600
Even if we're weak...

372
00:32:01,360 --> 00:32:03,650
Even if we can't sever
the demon's head...

373
00:32:04,610 --> 00:32:07,970
If we defeat one demon,
we can save dozens.

374
00:32:08,670 --> 00:32:11,119
And if we defeat an Upper Rank,

375
00:32:11,120 --> 00:32:14,000
we can save hundreds of people.

376
00:32:15,540 --> 00:32:17,730
It's not about whether we can or cannot.

377
00:32:19,330 --> 00:32:21,670
There are things we have to do.

378
00:32:27,050 --> 00:32:28,680
Are you angry?

379
00:32:30,550 --> 00:32:31,889
Yes.

380
00:32:31,890 --> 00:32:35,640
I am angry, Tanjiro.

381
00:32:36,260 --> 00:32:42,360
I have always been so angry.

382
00:32:44,900 --> 00:32:46,750
My parents were killed.

383
00:32:48,320 --> 00:32:50,110
My sister was killed.

384
00:32:51,660 --> 00:32:54,580
And except for Kanao,
all my Tsugukos were killed.

385
00:32:56,120 --> 00:32:58,120
Even those girls...

386
00:32:58,660 --> 00:33:00,919
If only...

387
00:33:00,920 --> 00:33:04,459
If only demons hadn't killed their family,

388
00:33:04,460 --> 00:33:07,340
they'd be living happily right now.

389
00:33:10,130 --> 00:33:13,329
It really pisses me off.

390
00:33:13,330 --> 00:33:15,850
Enough already, you piece of crap!

391
00:33:16,890 --> 00:33:20,390
Why doesn't poison work on him?

392
00:33:21,060 --> 00:33:22,690
You bastard!

393
00:33:34,240 --> 00:33:35,369
So admirable!

394
00:33:35,370 --> 00:33:36,909
You've tried so hard!

395
00:33:36,910 --> 00:33:39,369
I'm impressed.

396
00:33:39,370 --> 00:33:42,540
I never thought such a weak girl
would go this far.

397
00:33:43,500 --> 00:33:45,669
Even though you're not
as talented as your sister,

398
00:33:45,670 --> 00:33:48,100
you've done well as a demon hunter.

399
00:33:48,880 --> 00:33:51,730
It's a miracle you aren't dead yet.

400
00:33:54,300 --> 00:33:58,060
Even though it's all completely meaningless,
you're foolish enough to keep trying!

401
00:33:58,640 --> 00:34:00,639
This is the fragility of humanity!

402
00:34:00,640 --> 00:34:03,060
The beauty of humanity!

403
00:34:04,060 --> 00:34:06,780
You're worth being devoured by me.

404
00:34:07,820 --> 00:34:10,320
Let us live together forever!

405
00:34:13,610 --> 00:34:17,540
Do you have any last words?
I'm listening.

406
00:34:22,250 --> 00:34:25,080
Go to Hell.

407
00:34:30,300 --> 00:34:31,420
Master!

408
00:35:02,960 --> 00:35:05,330
He must be here too.

409
00:35:06,000 --> 00:35:10,250
Even he has to face me sooner or later.

410
00:35:17,260 --> 00:35:21,019
We tend to vaguely believe
that the people we love,

411
00:35:21,020 --> 00:35:22,679
the ones who matter to us,

412
00:35:22,680 --> 00:35:25,390
will still be around tomorrow,
and the day after that.

413
00:35:26,060 --> 00:35:29,979
But that's nothing more than a wish.

414
00:35:29,980 --> 00:35:31,730
Flower Breathing!

415
00:35:32,530 --> 00:35:36,279
It's not something that was
ever promised or guaranteed.

416
00:35:36,280 --> 00:35:37,490
Fourth Form:

417
00:35:38,990 --> 00:35:41,040
Crimson Hanagoromo!

418
00:35:47,290 --> 00:35:50,000
Wow, that was close.

419
00:35:53,840 --> 00:35:56,130
And yet, for some reason,

420
00:35:57,720 --> 00:36:03,140
we convince ourselves that
they will keep on living by our side.

421
00:36:06,230 --> 00:36:11,520
Please don't try to cut me
while I'm in the middle of absorbing.

422
00:36:20,160 --> 00:36:21,700
Oh?

423
00:36:22,160 --> 00:36:24,500
You're not taking the bait, I see.

424
00:36:25,450 --> 00:36:29,570
Is it because this girl
gave you a hand signal?

425
00:36:30,180 --> 00:36:33,050
Did she tell you about my powers?

426
00:36:33,670 --> 00:36:36,879
How impressive.
It was only a moment.

427
00:36:36,880 --> 00:36:41,140
Although it was pointless,
she was doing her best.

428
00:36:43,890 --> 00:36:46,770
But still,

429
00:36:47,360 --> 00:36:50,790
tonight's a beautiful night.

430
00:36:52,190 --> 00:36:57,120
Such fine treats keep coming
one after another.

431
00:36:58,160 --> 00:37:03,700
Really, what a beautiful night.

432
00:37:17,920 --> 00:37:21,090
You're there, aren't you?
Show yourself.

433
00:37:21,800 --> 00:37:23,930
I know you're there.

434
00:37:26,970 --> 00:37:32,100
Watch your tone
when you're talking to your senior.

435
00:37:32,860 --> 00:37:36,149
I see, you've improved a little.

436
00:37:36,150 --> 00:37:41,040
But you still look as scrawny as ever.

437
00:37:45,740 --> 00:37:50,030
It's been a while, Zenitsu.

438
00:37:52,660 --> 00:37:56,550
Kaigaku, now that you've
turned into a demon,

439
00:37:57,070 --> 00:38:00,590
I can no longer see you as my senior.

440
00:38:13,900 --> 00:38:16,590
Water Breathing, Ninth Form:

441
00:38:18,190 --> 00:38:20,490
Splashing Water Flow, Turbulent!

442
00:38:22,990 --> 00:38:24,239
Stay sharp!

443
00:38:24,240 --> 00:38:25,450
Got it!

444
00:38:26,490 --> 00:38:28,370
This realm is dangerous.

445
00:38:28,910 --> 00:38:32,740
The very buildings are throbbing
as if they're alive.

446
00:38:33,310 --> 00:38:36,170
It's trying to separate me from Giyu.

447
00:38:37,040 --> 00:38:39,759
We need to regroup with the other members

448
00:38:39,760 --> 00:38:42,470
and head straight for Muzan
without getting separated.

449
00:38:50,140 --> 00:38:54,020
Death report!
Shinobu Kocho is dead!

450
00:38:54,510 --> 00:38:58,940
She was killed in combat
with Upper Rank Two!

451
00:39:40,110 --> 00:39:41,529
The crow...

452
00:39:41,530 --> 00:39:44,189
What's the paper on its neck?

453
00:39:44,190 --> 00:39:46,320
The communication is unusually fast.

454
00:39:50,700 --> 00:39:52,619
Shinobu is dead.

455
00:39:52,620 --> 00:39:54,959
We mustn't look down in despair.

456
00:39:54,960 --> 00:39:57,550
Think about what needs
to be done next.

457
00:39:58,110 --> 00:39:59,250
Yes.

458
00:40:01,590 --> 00:40:05,340
What is the situation with the Hashiras
and other members?

459
00:40:06,720 --> 00:40:10,510
In the center of the 40th vertical
and the 12th horizontal layers,

460
00:40:12,220 --> 00:40:17,140
our troops are currently in battle
with demons, more than ten of them.

461
00:40:23,860 --> 00:40:28,160
And beyond that wall,
over thirty more demons are closing in.

462
00:40:34,580 --> 00:40:39,199
Yushiro's eyes can perceive
Blood Demon Arts visually,

463
00:40:39,200 --> 00:40:42,500
techniques that are invisible
to the human eye.

464
00:40:43,500 --> 00:40:45,379
These varying intensities of light

465
00:40:45,380 --> 00:40:49,090
likely represent the strength
of each Blood Demon Art.

466
00:40:49,890 --> 00:40:53,009
These buildings that move
and pulse like a living thing...

467
00:40:53,010 --> 00:40:56,140
They're also a manifestation
of such a technique.

468
00:40:56,680 --> 00:40:59,140
And it goes on endlessly.

469
00:41:02,060 --> 00:41:04,020
What incredible power.

470
00:41:05,280 --> 00:41:09,280
This demon castle can expand infinitely.

471
00:41:12,950 --> 00:41:17,200
We've been lured into a castle
that contains infinite demons.

472
00:41:21,380 --> 00:41:25,010
But we weren't just lured in
without a plan.

473
00:41:25,550 --> 00:41:29,340
Father prepared carefully for this day.

474
00:41:30,130 --> 00:41:32,389
Using Gyomei as the anchor point,

475
00:41:32,390 --> 00:41:36,009
he arranged the Hashiras
so they could rush in at any moment.

476
00:41:36,010 --> 00:41:39,099
He gave Kasugai crows the task
of connecting the scattered members,

477
00:41:39,100 --> 00:41:42,610
turning isolated points into lines,
and waited for the right moment.

478
00:41:43,890 --> 00:41:47,319
With help from Miss Tamayo and Yushiro,

479
00:41:47,320 --> 00:41:52,069
to complete the plan,

480
00:41:52,070 --> 00:41:57,450
our father and mother,
along with our sisters, gave their lives.

481
00:42:00,660 --> 00:42:04,210
We cannot afford to lose this battle.

482
00:42:10,510 --> 00:42:15,719
There are five massive forces
radiating through this vast space,

483
00:42:15,720 --> 00:42:18,389
as if to flaunt their power.

484
00:42:18,390 --> 00:42:20,680
These must be the Upper Ranks.

485
00:42:21,440 --> 00:42:25,480
One of them aligns exactly with
where Shinobu was last seen.

486
00:42:25,980 --> 00:42:27,109
An Upper Rank!

487
00:42:27,110 --> 00:42:30,489
Agatsuma has encountered Upper Rank Six!

488
00:42:30,490 --> 00:42:31,619
An Upper Rank?!

489
00:42:31,620 --> 00:42:33,249
Are there any other members with him?

490
00:42:33,250 --> 00:42:35,949
No one. Agatsuma is the only one there.

491
00:42:35,950 --> 00:42:38,659
A Hinoe-ranked member
couldn't handle an Upper Rank alone.

492
00:42:38,660 --> 00:42:40,160
Send reinforcements immediately!

493
00:42:46,790 --> 00:42:48,999
You haven't changed a bit.

494
00:42:49,000 --> 00:42:53,840
You're small and pathetic.
Still just as weak as ever.

495
00:42:54,340 --> 00:42:56,510
Aren't you gonna aim
to be a Hashira?

496
00:42:57,010 --> 00:42:59,520
Zenitsu.

497
00:43:00,350 --> 00:43:04,520
Can you use other forms
besides the First Form?

498
00:43:05,480 --> 00:43:09,319
Being put at the bottom
of the Upper Ranks, a mere placeholder,

499
00:43:09,320 --> 00:43:11,570
you sure seem happy.

500
00:43:15,320 --> 00:43:18,450
Now you can talk back, huh?

501
00:43:19,030 --> 00:43:21,870
Why did you become a demon?

502
00:43:22,910 --> 00:43:24,119
You wouldn't...

503
00:43:24,120 --> 00:43:26,499
Why would a Thunder Breathing successor

504
00:43:26,500 --> 00:43:28,040
become a damn demon?!

505
00:43:30,750 --> 00:43:33,009
Because you became a demon,

506
00:43:33,010 --> 00:43:34,340
Gramps...

507
00:43:35,970 --> 00:43:38,140
Gramps committed seppuku!

508
00:43:39,140 --> 00:43:43,100
Listen! He slit his belly all alone!

509
00:43:44,230 --> 00:43:46,350
No one there to deliver the final blow!

510
00:43:47,440 --> 00:43:51,149
When you cut your belly open
and there's no one to end it quickly,

511
00:43:51,150 --> 00:43:53,970
you suffer a slow, agonizing death!

512
00:43:54,480 --> 00:43:59,239
He let himself die in pain
without stabbing his own throat or heart!

513
00:43:59,240 --> 00:44:02,870
And it's all because a Thunder Breathing
user became a demon!

514
00:44:04,210 --> 00:44:06,669
I don't care.

515
00:44:06,670 --> 00:44:09,289
So what?

516
00:44:09,290 --> 00:44:13,339
Should I be sad? Should I repent?

517
00:44:13,340 --> 00:44:18,219
I don't give a damn about anyone
who doesn't recognize my worth.

518
00:44:18,220 --> 00:44:22,009
I always side with those, no matter what,

519
00:44:22,010 --> 00:44:25,280
who evaluate me correctly.

520
00:44:27,060 --> 00:44:31,319
If that old man died in agony,
then good riddance.

521
00:44:31,320 --> 00:44:34,439
After everything I did for him,

522
00:44:34,440 --> 00:44:36,739
he still refused to make me his successor,

523
00:44:36,740 --> 00:44:40,369
and instead, he made it a shared
inheritance with trash like you.

524
00:44:40,370 --> 00:44:42,030
That old bastard!

525
00:44:42,830 --> 00:44:44,949
He may have been a former Hashira,

526
00:44:44,950 --> 00:44:48,670
but I have no use for a senile old man.

527
00:44:53,500 --> 00:44:56,629
Gramps wasn't senile.

528
00:44:56,630 --> 00:44:59,720
If I'm trash, then you're scum.

529
00:45:00,190 --> 00:45:02,219
I can only use the First Form,

530
00:45:02,220 --> 00:45:05,220
and you can use all except the First Form.

531
00:45:05,810 --> 00:45:10,349
I feel sorry for Gramps for not
having a worthy successor at all!

532
00:45:10,350 --> 00:45:14,509
Don't lump me in with you!

533
00:45:14,510 --> 00:45:17,529
Thunder Breathing, Fourth Form:

534
00:45:17,530 --> 00:45:18,740
Distant Thunder!

535
00:45:26,830 --> 00:45:29,210
You're too slow, scum.

536
00:45:34,750 --> 00:45:36,299
I got cut.

537
00:45:36,300 --> 00:45:37,419
He's fast.

538
00:45:37,420 --> 00:45:39,129
He...

539
00:45:39,130 --> 00:45:42,720
He moves like a completely
different person.

540
00:45:44,850 --> 00:45:47,140
I ain't wrong.

541
00:45:57,530 --> 00:46:01,790
There is no shame in kneeling before
someone with overwhelming strength.

542
00:46:02,820 --> 00:46:06,200
As long as I stay alive,
it will work out somehow.

543
00:46:08,200 --> 00:46:11,160
I haven't lost until I die.

544
00:46:11,830 --> 00:46:15,089
Even if I rub my face in the dirt...

545
00:46:15,090 --> 00:46:17,049
Even if I lose my home...

546
00:46:17,050 --> 00:46:19,459
Even if I drink muddy water...

547
00:46:19,460 --> 00:46:22,690
Even if I get cursed for stealing money...

548
00:46:23,340 --> 00:46:27,139
As long as I live on,
I can win someday.

549
00:46:27,140 --> 00:46:28,809
I will win.

550
00:46:28,810 --> 00:46:31,730
I have moved forward
with that belief.

551
00:46:33,560 --> 00:46:35,360
Do you want to

552
00:46:36,230 --> 00:46:39,300
become a demon for greater strength?

553
00:46:40,030 --> 00:46:43,409
If My Lord recognizes you,

554
00:46:43,410 --> 00:46:46,140
you may become one of us.

555
00:46:50,410 --> 00:46:56,020
The stronger a swordsman,
the more time it takes to become a demon.

556
00:46:56,700 --> 00:46:59,760
It took me three days.

557
00:47:00,750 --> 00:47:04,629
For someone who can use a breathing
technique to become a demon,

558
00:47:04,630 --> 00:47:09,860
they must receive a great deal
of blood from My Lord.

559
00:47:10,800 --> 00:47:13,019
And rarely,

560
00:47:13,020 --> 00:47:17,610
there are those whose constitution
does not allow them to become a demon.

561
00:47:18,360 --> 00:47:21,440
But what about you?

562
00:47:25,450 --> 00:47:27,630
That is blood to be grateful for.

563
00:47:28,120 --> 00:47:32,350
You must not spill even a single drop.

564
00:47:33,160 --> 00:47:35,619
If you do,

565
00:47:35,620 --> 00:47:40,880
Your head and body shall bid
each other a tearful farewell.

566
00:47:45,970 --> 00:47:49,509
That fear made the cells
throughout my body

567
00:47:49,510 --> 00:47:52,580
scream and burst into tears.

568
00:47:57,270 --> 00:47:59,359
Compared to that,

569
00:47:59,360 --> 00:48:02,800
this small fry is nothing.

570
00:48:03,340 --> 00:48:07,030
He may have gained some strength,
but he can't match an Upper Rank.

571
00:48:07,740 --> 00:48:11,279
Zenitsu Agatsuma is just a trash.

572
00:48:11,280 --> 00:48:13,789
He's always sobbing.

573
00:48:13,790 --> 00:48:16,669
A guy without dignity and guts.

574
00:48:16,670 --> 00:48:20,629
Help me! I fell into a pitfall!

575
00:48:20,630 --> 00:48:23,090
I sprained my leg!

576
00:48:23,710 --> 00:48:29,430
And that old bastard said this trash
and I would be successors together.

577
00:48:29,890 --> 00:48:31,930
Take this, Kaigaku.

578
00:48:32,560 --> 00:48:34,430
Gramps!

579
00:48:35,060 --> 00:48:37,920
Isn't this too big?

580
00:48:38,400 --> 00:48:40,169
- Make smaller, Gramps.
- You and I are the same?

581
00:48:40,170 --> 00:48:42,400
- Quit complaining!
- You and I are the same?

582
00:48:44,230 --> 00:48:46,900
Like hell we are!

583
00:48:48,410 --> 00:48:51,359
It's only natural that he should die!

584
00:48:51,360 --> 00:48:53,539
Not only him, but also you!

585
00:48:53,540 --> 00:48:55,890
You two should die!

586
00:48:57,040 --> 00:49:00,290
I could only ever master the First Form,

587
00:49:00,830 --> 00:49:04,420
and you mastered every form
except the First Form.

588
00:49:06,420 --> 00:49:08,469
That's why

589
00:49:08,470 --> 00:49:13,970
Gramps made us the successors
of Thunder Breathing together.

590
00:49:15,760 --> 00:49:17,440
But you...

591
00:49:18,350 --> 00:49:22,290
You turned into a demon
just to reject that.

592
00:49:24,980 --> 00:49:25,899
He's coming!

593
00:49:25,900 --> 00:49:28,450
Thunder Breathing, Second Form:

594
00:49:29,280 --> 00:49:30,780
Rice Spirit!

595
00:49:32,910 --> 00:49:35,540
Five consecutive attacks in one breath
in the blink of an eye.

596
00:49:38,750 --> 00:49:40,579
So you have eaten people!

597
00:49:40,580 --> 00:49:43,789
You can't already tell the difference
between right and wrong, huh?!

598
00:49:43,790 --> 00:49:46,340
I sure can tell right from wrong.

599
00:49:47,840 --> 00:49:49,219
What's the matter?

600
00:49:49,220 --> 00:49:52,320
Weren't you the old man's favorite?

601
00:49:53,340 --> 00:49:59,010
Why don't you hurry up and show me
what the old man so graciously taught you?

602
00:50:02,850 --> 00:50:04,229
Come on!

603
00:50:04,230 --> 00:50:06,339
Don't hold back!

604
00:50:06,340 --> 00:50:08,780
Attack me with everything you've got!

605
00:50:14,950 --> 00:50:16,620
Thunder Breathing,

606
00:50:18,950 --> 00:50:20,410
First Form:

607
00:50:22,580 --> 00:50:24,290
Thunderclap and Flash.

608
00:50:30,340 --> 00:50:35,469
You think I'd get hit by such a basic form,
charging straight at me,

609
00:50:35,470 --> 00:50:37,100
like a fool?!

610
00:50:38,900 --> 00:50:42,099
Thunder Breathing, Third Form:

611
00:50:42,100 --> 00:50:43,690
Thunder Swarm!

612
00:50:49,320 --> 00:50:51,899
A wavelike attack while spinning!

613
00:50:51,900 --> 00:50:53,409
What's wrong?

614
00:50:53,410 --> 00:50:55,650
Is that all you've got?!

615
00:50:56,990 --> 00:50:59,329
Thunder Breathing, First Form:

616
00:50:59,330 --> 00:51:01,260
Thunderclap and Flash—Eightfold!

617
00:51:05,830 --> 00:51:07,670
It won't work!

618
00:51:08,840 --> 00:51:12,010
Thunder Breathing, Fifth Form:

619
00:51:14,260 --> 00:51:15,840
Heat Lightning!

620
00:51:17,550 --> 00:51:18,930
How's that?

621
00:51:19,560 --> 00:51:23,140
That's the sharpness of my blade
infused with Blood Demon Art.

622
00:51:23,580 --> 00:51:28,430
A slashing attack that cracks
and burns your skin and flesh.

623
00:51:29,150 --> 00:51:32,900
Those who evaluate me correctly
and know my worth are right.

624
00:51:33,450 --> 00:51:36,660
And those who evaluate me poorly
are wrong.

625
00:51:37,280 --> 00:51:40,720
Do you get it now?
This is my power!

626
00:51:41,240 --> 00:51:43,580
The me who has become a demon!

627
00:51:44,060 --> 00:51:46,249
Whether it's a single or an eightfold,

628
00:51:46,250 --> 00:51:49,169
if that's all you can do,
then calling you a successor

629
00:51:49,170 --> 00:51:51,210
was a huge mistake!

630
00:51:58,260 --> 00:52:02,430
So this is your answer, huh?

631
00:52:03,930 --> 00:52:05,979
I knew it.

632
00:52:05,980 --> 00:52:07,730
I knew it, but still...

633
00:52:12,860 --> 00:52:17,069
Zenitsu, this is your end!

634
00:52:17,070 --> 00:52:19,070
Thunder Breathing,

635
00:52:20,160 --> 00:52:21,650
Sixth Form:

636
00:52:30,500 --> 00:52:32,999
Rumble and Flash!

637
00:52:33,000 --> 00:52:36,929
The slashes you took will keep
cracking through your body!

638
00:52:36,930 --> 00:52:40,929
Burn my power
into your eyes and flesh!

639
00:52:40,930 --> 00:52:44,430
I became a demon
and surpassed Thunder Breathing!

640
00:52:48,520 --> 00:52:52,149
I'm special! I'm different from you!

641
00:52:52,150 --> 00:52:54,900
I'm different from you all!

642
00:52:55,340 --> 00:52:58,910
Looks like the old man was dead wrong
about you after all!

643
00:53:03,240 --> 00:53:05,870
Learn from Kaigaku's example!

644
00:53:06,410 --> 00:53:09,310
Be like your senior disciple!

645
00:53:10,040 --> 00:53:11,919
In Thunder Breathing,

646
00:53:11,920 --> 00:53:14,749
the First Form is the foundation
of all the forms, right?

647
00:53:14,750 --> 00:53:17,419
If you can't use the First Form,
in the end...

648
00:53:17,420 --> 00:53:19,839
You know... Right?

649
00:53:19,840 --> 00:53:23,719
Even if you can use the other forms,
it doesn't mean much.

650
00:53:23,720 --> 00:53:27,849
And yet, that Kaigaku guy is so arrogant.

651
00:53:27,850 --> 00:53:30,349
He cannot become a Hashira.

652
00:53:30,350 --> 00:53:32,480
He'll probably die soon anyway.

653
00:53:33,550 --> 00:53:35,520
What did you do that for?

654
00:53:37,120 --> 00:53:39,950
I heard you hit a higher-ranking member.

655
00:53:40,580 --> 00:53:42,910
Don't cause problems, you trash!

656
00:53:43,490 --> 00:53:47,090
Having someone like you around
is a real disgrace.

657
00:53:49,540 --> 00:53:54,269
I can fully understand that
Kaigaku hates me.

658
00:53:54,270 --> 00:53:56,750
After all, I hate him too.

659
00:53:57,860 --> 00:54:01,740
But I respected you
from the bottom of my heart.

660
00:54:02,450 --> 00:54:05,680
You worked hard and were truly dedicated.

661
00:54:06,310 --> 00:54:10,390
I was always looking at your back.

662
00:54:11,230 --> 00:54:14,190
You were special.

663
00:54:15,230 --> 00:54:19,540
To Gramps and me,
you were special and important.

664
00:54:20,540 --> 00:54:24,070
But that wasn't enough for you.

665
00:54:24,660 --> 00:54:29,500
I could always hear the sound
of dissatisfaction coming from you.

666
00:54:31,710 --> 00:54:36,420
The happiness box in your heart
has a hole in it.

667
00:54:37,840 --> 00:54:40,380
And the happiness inside it
is constantly spilling out.

668
00:54:41,880 --> 00:54:44,799
If you don't find that hole
and plug it up,

669
00:54:44,800 --> 00:54:46,680
you'll never be satisfied.

670
00:54:49,390 --> 00:54:52,450
Gramps, I'm sorry.

671
00:54:53,480 --> 00:54:55,140
Our paths...

672
00:54:56,610 --> 00:54:57,890
have gone separate ways.

673
00:55:09,540 --> 00:55:11,370
He has strength left?

674
00:55:20,630 --> 00:55:22,880
The heck?

675
00:55:30,670 --> 00:55:34,020
Forgive me, my senior disciple.

676
00:55:53,750 --> 00:55:56,940
Thunder Breathing, Seventh Form:

677
00:56:00,370 --> 00:56:02,340
Honoikazuchi-no-Kami.

678
00:56:09,840 --> 00:56:13,599
I... I couldn't see that.

679
00:56:13,600 --> 00:56:16,140
What was that technique?

680
00:56:16,640 --> 00:56:18,269
It was so fast.

681
00:56:18,270 --> 00:56:19,939
I don't know that form.

682
00:56:19,940 --> 00:56:21,570
What did he use?!

683
00:56:22,100 --> 00:56:24,739
Shit! Damnit!

684
00:56:24,740 --> 00:56:27,699
I knew it, that old man favored you!

685
00:56:27,700 --> 00:56:31,079
He only taught you,
and didn't teach me!

686
00:56:31,080 --> 00:56:32,540
You're wrong.

687
00:56:34,870 --> 00:56:37,470
Gramps wasn't that kind of person.

688
00:56:38,420 --> 00:56:41,040
It's my own form.

689
00:56:41,670 --> 00:56:44,630
A form I came up with myself.

690
00:56:45,630 --> 00:56:47,010
With this technique...

691
00:56:47,880 --> 00:56:52,940
I dreamed of the day
I could fight alongside you.

692
00:56:56,600 --> 00:56:58,860
The Seventh Form, he said?

693
00:56:59,790 --> 00:57:03,019
From Thunder Breathing,
which only has six forms,

694
00:57:03,020 --> 00:57:05,230
he developed a seventh?

695
00:57:06,240 --> 00:57:07,739
He did?

696
00:57:07,740 --> 00:57:10,110
The guy who can only use the First Form?

697
00:57:11,280 --> 00:57:14,240
A piece of trash
who was always beneath me?

698
00:57:15,830 --> 00:57:18,639
It's unbearable! I won't accept it!

699
00:57:18,640 --> 00:57:21,419
I can't accept this truth!

700
00:57:21,420 --> 00:57:25,250
How could I lose to someone like him?

701
00:57:26,210 --> 00:57:28,800
I feel like I'm going insane.

702
00:57:30,380 --> 00:57:31,550
Hold on.

703
00:57:32,470 --> 00:57:34,509
No, I haven't lost.

704
00:57:34,510 --> 00:57:36,889
That trash will die from falling.

705
00:57:36,890 --> 00:57:39,770
I bet he doesn't have any strength left.

706
00:57:40,440 --> 00:57:42,860
He's going to die with me.

707
00:57:44,480 --> 00:57:48,800
Someone who never gives to others will be
unable to receive anything from them.

708
00:57:50,660 --> 00:57:55,489
In the end, only wanting
is the same as having nothing.

709
00:57:55,490 --> 00:57:58,340
Because you're unable
to create anything.

710
00:57:59,960 --> 00:58:02,820
How pathetic to die alone.

711
00:58:25,060 --> 00:58:26,440
What is this place?

712
00:58:34,740 --> 00:58:36,220
Gramps!

713
00:58:38,950 --> 00:58:42,869
Sorry, I couldn't get along with Kaigaku.

714
00:58:42,870 --> 00:58:47,340
I wrote letters to him,
but he never replied.

715
00:58:48,340 --> 00:58:49,669
If I weren't around,

716
00:58:49,670 --> 00:58:52,629
Kaigaku might not have
turned out that way.

717
00:58:52,630 --> 00:58:55,340
I'm really sorry! Forgive me!

718
00:58:55,840 --> 00:58:58,639
I'm sorry I couldn't return the favor!

719
00:58:58,640 --> 00:59:03,379
I wanted to become a Hashira too
while you were still alive, but...

720
00:59:03,380 --> 00:59:04,849
Sorry!

721
00:59:04,850 --> 00:59:06,590
Gramps, I'm sorry!

722
00:59:10,440 --> 00:59:12,570
Do you hate me now?

723
00:59:13,150 --> 00:59:15,570
Please say something, Gramps!

724
00:59:17,240 --> 00:59:19,289
Curses! What's this?

725
00:59:19,290 --> 00:59:20,910
It's wrapping around my feet.

726
00:59:22,250 --> 00:59:25,210
Gramps, I... I...

727
00:59:27,540 --> 00:59:29,300
Damnit!

728
00:59:31,170 --> 00:59:32,840
Zenitsu.

729
00:59:40,390 --> 00:59:44,350
You are my pride and joy.

730
01:00:07,420 --> 01:00:09,999
How is he? Can he be saved?

731
01:00:10,000 --> 01:00:13,129
I know him! Do something!

732
01:00:13,130 --> 01:00:14,879
I'm begging you!

733
01:00:14,880 --> 01:00:17,179
Just shut the heck up, Murata.

734
01:00:17,180 --> 01:00:19,849
You're just dead weight.

735
01:00:19,850 --> 01:00:22,740
Watch our surroundings
so we don't get attacked.

736
01:00:24,080 --> 01:00:26,269
Hey! What rank are you?!

737
01:00:26,270 --> 01:00:28,810
I won't forgive you if you're lower!

738
01:00:29,380 --> 01:00:32,860
I'm a demon, of course
I don't have a rank.

739
01:00:33,730 --> 01:00:35,569
I've applied a Demon Styptic,

740
01:00:35,570 --> 01:00:40,320
but if these cracks on his face keep spreading,
they'll split through to his eyes.

741
01:00:41,080 --> 01:00:42,620
You hear me?

742
01:00:46,830 --> 01:00:49,579
Don't freak someone out
who's already in bad shape!

743
01:00:49,580 --> 01:00:52,919
I've used a coagulant too,
but the bleeding won't stop.

744
01:00:52,920 --> 01:00:54,209
Don't say it!

745
01:00:54,210 --> 01:00:56,299
You're gonna be all right!
You'll be saved!

746
01:00:56,300 --> 01:00:58,089
We won't let you die!

747
01:00:58,090 --> 01:00:59,179
Hang it there, Agatsuma!

748
01:00:59,180 --> 01:01:00,850
Hang in there! Hang in there!

749
01:01:01,550 --> 01:01:07,659
The Upper Rank you fought against
hadn't mastered his techniques and abilities.

750
01:01:07,660 --> 01:01:09,900
What a lucky guy.

751
01:01:10,440 --> 01:01:13,680
If you had fought him a year from now,
you would have been killed instantly.

752
01:01:15,740 --> 01:01:19,910
Stop saying such depressing things!

753
01:01:26,410 --> 01:01:29,370
I didn't say anything wrong.

754
01:01:31,670 --> 01:01:32,919
What?

755
01:01:32,920 --> 01:01:35,760
That loud mouth of yours
just brought a demon right to us.

756
01:01:37,630 --> 01:01:39,300
You're its perfect target.

757
01:01:40,800 --> 01:01:42,889
Yushiro, was it?

758
01:01:42,890 --> 01:01:44,809
I leave Agatsuma to you!

759
01:01:44,810 --> 01:01:46,390
Attack!

760
01:01:49,230 --> 01:01:51,679
Hurry up and defeat it, Senior.

761
01:01:51,680 --> 01:01:54,069
I'll get you for this!

762
01:01:54,070 --> 01:01:55,110
Crap!

763
01:01:56,980 --> 01:01:59,399
Water Breathing, Second Form:

764
01:01:59,400 --> 01:02:00,779
Water Wheel!

765
01:02:00,780 --> 01:02:02,450
Take this!

766
01:02:03,870 --> 01:02:07,120
I'll go around! You take that side!

767
01:02:23,840 --> 01:02:27,010
This is bad.
They will encounter each other.

768
01:02:30,230 --> 01:02:32,849
We're not encountering any Upper Ranks.

769
01:02:32,850 --> 01:02:35,559
Are Muzan's whereabouts still far away?

770
01:02:35,560 --> 01:02:37,580
Is everyone else all right?

771
01:02:40,570 --> 01:02:42,240
Shinobu...

772
01:02:43,110 --> 01:02:45,099
We will win for sure.

773
01:02:45,100 --> 01:02:48,050
All of us... We will!

774
01:02:50,870 --> 01:02:52,370
What is this shaking?

775
01:02:52,900 --> 01:02:54,459
Giyu!

776
01:02:54,460 --> 01:02:55,869
Stop!

777
01:02:55,870 --> 01:02:57,250
Calm down.

778
01:02:59,170 --> 01:03:01,469
Is someone still fighting?

779
01:03:01,470 --> 01:03:03,630
Is someone gonna die again?

780
01:03:09,310 --> 01:03:11,729
No, it's not.

781
01:03:11,730 --> 01:03:13,770
Is it coming this way?

782
01:03:16,400 --> 01:03:18,940
I know this smell.

783
01:03:27,370 --> 01:03:28,199
Above!

784
01:03:28,200 --> 01:03:29,160
Tanjiro, get back!

785
01:03:33,870 --> 01:03:35,950
Long time no see.

786
01:03:37,590 --> 01:03:43,800
I'm surprised a weakling
like you is still alive.

787
01:03:45,090 --> 01:03:47,970
Tanjiro Kamado!

788
01:03:50,100 --> 01:03:53,020
Akaza!

789
01:04:25,630 --> 01:04:30,679
Most likely, inside this cocoon of flesh,

790
01:04:30,680 --> 01:04:34,890
he's breaking down the medicine
that turns demons back into humans.

791
01:04:35,520 --> 01:04:37,519
Muzan Kibutsuji...

792
01:04:37,520 --> 01:04:41,940
You're the one we absolutely must destroy.

793
01:04:42,920 --> 01:04:46,530
And yet, no matter what I do...

794
01:04:54,540 --> 01:04:58,040
Eventually, I'll be absorbed too.

795
01:04:58,870 --> 01:05:03,180
Please, someone, come quickly.

796
01:05:04,170 --> 01:05:05,590
Please...

797
01:05:19,980 --> 01:05:22,189
According to Father's theory,

798
01:05:22,190 --> 01:05:25,360
if Muzan dies, the other demons
will perish as well.

799
01:05:26,930 --> 01:05:30,700
That means Muzan Kibutsuji is still alive.

800
01:05:32,280 --> 01:05:36,660
His power is probably being
held back by Miss Tamayo.

801
01:05:37,660 --> 01:05:39,789
Because it's being suppressed,

802
01:05:39,790 --> 01:05:42,420
he isn't reacting to Yushiro's vision.

803
01:05:43,460 --> 01:05:46,659
Before his power returns,

804
01:05:46,660 --> 01:05:49,120
we must defeat him, no matter what.

805
01:05:51,090 --> 01:05:56,560
Still, inside this Infinity Castle...

806
01:05:57,060 --> 01:06:01,180
Can we really find Muzan Kibutsuji?

807
01:06:06,530 --> 01:06:11,310
No need to rush.
You're doing well.

808
01:06:13,370 --> 01:06:16,500
He will show himself.

809
01:06:17,240 --> 01:06:19,790
His coming to me is the proof.

810
01:06:22,040 --> 01:06:26,670
That's the kind of man Muzan Kibutsuji is.

811
01:06:32,220 --> 01:06:34,430
I understand, Father.

812
01:06:35,010 --> 01:06:37,180
I'll definitely see it through.

813
01:06:39,180 --> 01:06:42,689
Before our members reach their limits,

814
01:06:42,690 --> 01:06:44,940
we must find and end him.

815
01:06:56,120 --> 01:06:57,789
Be their shield!

816
01:06:57,790 --> 01:06:59,039
We'll hold the line

817
01:06:59,040 --> 01:07:02,749
and minimize the Hashiras' exhaustion!

818
01:07:02,750 --> 01:07:03,619
Go ahead!

819
01:07:03,620 --> 01:07:05,170
Please keep moving forward!

820
01:07:05,710 --> 01:07:07,859
Stone Hashira, hurry and go!

821
01:07:07,860 --> 01:07:08,960
You all...

822
01:07:17,470 --> 01:07:19,969
Please must defeat Kibutsuji for us!

823
01:07:19,970 --> 01:07:21,480
We're counting on you!

824
01:07:22,100 --> 01:07:23,709
I hear you.

825
01:07:23,710 --> 01:07:26,359
I leave this place to you all.

826
01:07:26,360 --> 01:07:27,690
Tokito!

827
01:07:29,230 --> 01:07:33,500
Time to show off everything
we learned during Hashira Training!

828
01:07:41,830 --> 01:07:44,190
Thank you, everyone.

829
01:07:44,850 --> 01:07:48,669
Father, everyone is doing their best.

830
01:07:48,670 --> 01:07:53,630
CONFIRMED MULTIPLE PEOPLE ARE INJURED
AND CONFIRMED PRESENCE OF DEMONS

831
01:07:59,060 --> 01:08:00,680
Don't cry.

832
01:08:01,270 --> 01:08:03,220
You must not stop your hands.

833
01:08:03,810 --> 01:08:06,060
We will not lose.

834
01:08:07,860 --> 01:08:08,980
Yes.

835
01:08:12,190 --> 01:08:15,460
Lord Kiriya is truly admirable.

836
01:08:16,610 --> 01:08:20,029
Even with the pain of losing
his father still fresh,

837
01:08:20,030 --> 01:08:22,200
he has taken command of the Corps

838
01:08:22,950 --> 01:08:26,380
and is determined to fulfill his duty.

839
01:08:27,750 --> 01:08:30,450
Don't you agree, Rengoku?

840
01:08:31,710 --> 01:08:33,300
You're right.

841
01:08:34,920 --> 01:08:40,930
If children so young have such courage,
I shall stake my life to protect them,

842
01:08:41,930 --> 01:08:44,479
just as Kyojuro did,

843
01:08:44,480 --> 01:08:50,180
so I will not bring shame
to the name of the Rengoku family.

844
01:09:03,200 --> 01:09:06,160
She seems to be suffering.

845
01:09:07,500 --> 01:09:13,169
I used the medicine provided by Tamayo,
a demon who was cooperating with Master,

846
01:09:13,170 --> 01:09:16,130
as I was told, but...

847
01:09:17,760 --> 01:09:23,510
Will Nezuko really become human again?

848
01:09:24,100 --> 01:09:27,099
If Nezuko returns to being human,

849
01:09:27,100 --> 01:09:30,479
Muzan's entire plan will collapse.

850
01:09:30,480 --> 01:09:32,519
His pursuit spanning
over a thousand years...

851
01:09:32,520 --> 01:09:36,989
His dream of a perfect form
will be shattered.

852
01:09:36,990 --> 01:09:41,910
The conquest of sunlight
will be reset to square one.

853
01:09:43,870 --> 01:09:47,409
The only demon who hasn't
been burnt by sunlight,

854
01:09:47,410 --> 01:09:50,169
in all these long centuries,

855
01:09:50,170 --> 01:09:53,040
is Nezuko.

856
01:10:08,520 --> 01:10:13,920
The word "endgame"
keeps crossing my mind.

857
01:10:17,220 --> 01:10:22,780
Every time I do, I tremble inside
and my heart beats faster.

858
01:10:23,660 --> 01:10:28,120
This long battle might finally
come to an end tonight.

859
01:10:28,910 --> 01:10:33,750
I can't believe I'm still alive
to witness it.

860
01:10:34,850 --> 01:10:36,399
Tanjiro...

861
01:10:36,400 --> 01:10:37,589
When I think about it,

862
01:10:37,590 --> 01:10:41,520
ever since you brought your sister
who had become a demon,

863
01:10:42,130 --> 01:10:48,100
I felt as though large cogs
have been turning.

864
01:10:49,540 --> 01:10:55,780
If everything built up through the battles
so far were a massive machine,

865
01:10:56,400 --> 01:11:02,460
then when the two small cogs that are you
and Nezuko were fitted into place,

866
01:11:03,090 --> 01:11:08,420
the once-stalled situation
suddenly began to shift.

867
01:11:11,580 --> 01:11:14,080
Don't lose, Nezuko.

868
01:11:15,500 --> 01:11:18,170
Don't lose, Tanjiro.

869
01:11:19,200 --> 01:11:22,340
You must not lose.

870
01:11:22,780 --> 01:11:24,180
Hinokami Kagura:

871
01:11:24,670 --> 01:11:25,890
Fire Wheel!

872
01:11:28,720 --> 01:11:30,389
Come on! Come on! Come on!

873
01:11:30,390 --> 01:11:32,930
If I can't cut his arm,
then I can't sever his head.

874
01:11:39,630 --> 01:11:40,899
I did it.

875
01:11:40,900 --> 01:11:42,689
And I dodged his attack.

876
01:11:42,690 --> 01:11:45,199
That means I can fight him.

877
01:11:45,200 --> 01:11:48,490
I couldn't aim for his neck,
but next time...!

878
01:11:49,660 --> 01:11:51,239
Hinokami Kagura:

879
01:11:51,240 --> 01:11:52,560
Fake Rainbow.

880
01:12:07,720 --> 01:12:09,299
Tanjiro...

881
01:12:09,300 --> 01:12:12,140
You've refined your techniques
to an exceptional degree.

882
01:12:13,420 --> 01:12:18,190
It's no exaggeration to say your strength
is equal to a Hashira's.

883
01:12:18,770 --> 01:12:22,110
You're fighting well
against the Upper Rank Three.

884
01:12:28,200 --> 01:12:32,080
That snowy day,
you were overwhelmed by despair,

885
01:12:32,610 --> 01:12:38,800
you bowed your head, with nothing left
but tears and a plea for your sister's life.

886
01:12:46,720 --> 01:12:48,880
And now you can fight.

887
01:12:50,010 --> 01:12:55,100
So you won't lose your life
or your dignity.

888
01:12:56,940 --> 01:12:59,729
"This boy isn't weak."

889
01:12:59,730 --> 01:13:01,939
"Don't insult him."

890
01:13:01,940 --> 01:13:06,030
Now I admit Kyojuro's words were true.

891
01:13:06,480 --> 01:13:09,199
You certainly weren't weak.

892
01:13:09,200 --> 01:13:11,120
You have my respect.

893
01:13:14,700 --> 01:13:16,960
Technique Development.

894
01:13:21,540 --> 01:13:24,130
Shall we begin?

895
01:13:24,840 --> 01:13:26,990
It's time to have some fun.

896
01:14:13,350 --> 01:14:16,599
Water Breathing, Third Form:

897
01:14:16,600 --> 01:14:18,270
Flowing Dance!

898
01:14:19,100 --> 01:14:21,099
So you are the Water Hashira.

899
01:14:21,100 --> 01:14:23,019
Perfect!

900
01:14:23,020 --> 01:14:25,690
It's been fifty years
since I've encountered one.

901
01:14:33,740 --> 01:14:36,580
Destructive Death, Disorder!

902
01:14:38,790 --> 01:14:41,620
Water Breathing, Eleventh Form:

903
01:14:42,500 --> 01:14:43,420
Dead Calm.

904
01:14:48,840 --> 01:14:51,469
I've never seen that technique.

905
01:14:51,470 --> 01:14:56,469
The last Water Hashira I killed
didn't use that.

906
01:14:56,470 --> 01:14:59,560
Hinokami Kagura: Raging Sun!

907
01:15:01,850 --> 01:15:03,020
He's gone?

908
01:15:03,810 --> 01:15:05,059
Behind me!

909
01:15:05,060 --> 01:15:07,070
Hinokami Kagura: Fake Rain—

910
01:15:07,980 --> 01:15:10,899
Water Breathing, Second Form:

911
01:15:10,900 --> 01:15:12,320
Water Wheel.

912
01:15:24,670 --> 01:15:26,210
Hinokami Kagura:

913
01:15:27,500 --> 01:15:28,919
Flame Dance!

914
01:15:28,920 --> 01:15:31,209
Destructive Death, Leg Type:

915
01:15:31,210 --> 01:15:33,340
Crown Splitter!

916
01:15:34,050 --> 01:15:36,220
I did it... Blocked it with my sword.

917
01:15:40,600 --> 01:15:42,019
Did it graze me?

918
01:15:42,020 --> 01:15:44,980
Just barely, and it had such force.

919
01:15:49,340 --> 01:15:50,820
Elegant!

920
01:15:52,610 --> 01:15:56,069
Such refined swordsmanship!
Truly magnificent!

921
01:15:56,070 --> 01:15:59,439
State your name!
What is your name?

922
01:15:59,440 --> 01:16:01,040
I want to remember it.

923
01:16:03,200 --> 01:16:05,959
A demon isn't worth hearing my name.

924
01:16:05,960 --> 01:16:09,000
I hate talking, so don't talk to me.

925
01:16:09,920 --> 01:16:14,049
Oh, you hate talking.

926
01:16:14,050 --> 01:16:16,299
Well, I love talking.

927
01:16:16,300 --> 01:16:18,429
I'm gonna ask your name

928
01:16:18,430 --> 01:16:20,380
over and over!

929
01:16:26,730 --> 01:16:29,939
Destructive Death, Leg Type:

930
01:16:29,940 --> 01:16:32,400
Explosive Flurry!

931
01:16:44,870 --> 01:16:46,250
Giyu!

932
01:16:47,790 --> 01:16:52,300
I see, so his name is Giyu.

933
01:16:55,840 --> 01:16:57,549
Hinokami Kagura:

934
01:16:57,550 --> 01:17:00,509
Destructive Death,
Eight-Layered Demon Core!

935
01:17:00,510 --> 01:17:02,390
Burning Bones, Summer Sun!

936
01:17:17,860 --> 01:17:19,989
Nice moves.

937
01:17:19,990 --> 01:17:23,869
You've trained remarkably well
in such a short time.

938
01:17:23,870 --> 01:17:25,829
You have my compliments.

939
01:17:25,830 --> 01:17:30,509
That said, Kyojuro did good work.

940
01:17:30,510 --> 01:17:36,419
That night, you were a total weakling,
rolling on the ground.

941
01:17:36,420 --> 01:17:39,089
Nothing more than a weed.

942
01:17:39,090 --> 01:17:43,009
But look at you now!

943
01:17:43,010 --> 01:17:45,309
Your growth is stunning!

944
01:17:45,310 --> 01:17:49,980
I'm genuinely happy.
I can feel my heart racing.

945
01:17:52,480 --> 01:17:56,260
It's good that Kyojuro
died that night.

946
01:17:58,900 --> 01:18:03,199
Had he lived, he might not
have grown any stronger.

947
01:18:03,200 --> 01:18:08,580
Because he clung to foolish values,
like wanting to remain human.

948
01:18:09,750 --> 01:18:11,460
What did you say?

949
01:18:18,510 --> 01:18:21,860
You... Don't you say another word.

950
01:18:25,600 --> 01:18:28,460
Don't say another word
about Rengoku.

951
01:18:29,570 --> 01:18:33,439
Why? I'm praising him, you know.

952
01:18:33,440 --> 01:18:37,069
Both you and Kyojuro.

953
01:18:37,070 --> 01:18:40,779
No, you're just insulting.

954
01:18:40,780 --> 01:18:43,199
All you're doing is spitting in disgust.

955
01:18:43,200 --> 01:18:44,800
At everyone.

956
01:18:45,950 --> 01:18:48,539
You misunderstand, Tanjiro.

957
01:18:48,540 --> 01:18:53,300
I only despise the weak.

958
01:18:53,860 --> 01:18:57,960
I only spit in disgust at weaklings.

959
01:18:58,630 --> 01:19:00,689
Right.

960
01:19:00,690 --> 01:19:03,680
The weak disgust me.

961
01:19:04,140 --> 01:19:05,740
They make me sick.

962
01:19:07,010 --> 01:19:11,390
Being weeded out is nothing more
than nature's law.

963
01:19:12,390 --> 01:19:15,440
Everything you're saying
is completely wrong.

964
01:19:18,940 --> 01:19:22,860
The fact that you're standing here
right now is proof enough.

965
01:19:24,360 --> 01:19:27,239
Everyone is born weak,
just a helpless baby.

966
01:19:27,240 --> 01:19:29,870
We all need someone to help us
survive at the start.

967
01:19:30,480 --> 01:19:32,580
You were the same, Akaza.

968
01:19:33,790 --> 01:19:36,079
Maybe you don't remember,

969
01:19:36,080 --> 01:19:40,300
but when you were a baby,
someone protected you, helped you,

970
01:19:40,780 --> 01:19:42,340
and that's why you're alive today.

971
01:19:47,250 --> 01:19:50,469
The strong are meant to protect
and help the weak.

972
01:19:50,470 --> 01:19:52,679
And the weak grow stronger,

973
01:19:52,680 --> 01:19:55,940
so that one day, they can protect
someone else in turn.

974
01:19:56,400 --> 01:19:58,440
That is the law of nature.

975
01:19:59,190 --> 01:20:03,319
Akaza, I can't accept
your way of thinking.

976
01:20:03,320 --> 01:20:06,990
I won't let you do
whatever you want any longer!

977
01:20:11,910 --> 01:20:14,220
Now I understand.

978
01:20:17,080 --> 01:20:21,390
I can't stand this guy,
from the very core of my being.

979
01:20:22,340 --> 01:20:25,840
Even now that he's strong,
this feeling doesn't go away.

980
01:20:30,560 --> 01:20:35,040
No matter what you say,
everyone is a baby at first.

981
01:20:35,620 --> 01:20:38,900
You get help from others
and gradually learn.

982
01:20:39,770 --> 01:20:42,779
Don't compare yourself to other people.

983
01:20:42,780 --> 01:20:46,190
You're always fighting yourself.

984
01:20:46,820 --> 01:20:50,860
What's important is becoming
stronger than yesterday.

985
01:20:52,080 --> 01:20:55,539
Keep doing that for
ten or twenty years,

986
01:20:55,540 --> 01:20:57,709
and you'll become something remarkable.

987
01:20:57,710 --> 01:21:02,320
And then, you will help other people.

988
01:21:10,050 --> 01:21:11,009
What?

989
01:21:11,010 --> 01:21:13,200
He just swung at empty air.

990
01:21:19,100 --> 01:21:24,530
Tanjiro, you are really unpleasant.

991
01:21:25,610 --> 01:21:28,239
Destructive Death, Crushing Type:

992
01:21:28,240 --> 01:21:30,560
Ten Thousand Leaves Flashing Willow!

993
01:21:33,700 --> 01:21:35,749
He's incredibly fast.

994
01:21:35,750 --> 01:21:38,619
No, he's more than fast.

995
01:21:38,620 --> 01:21:41,169
This feeling and this accuracy...

996
01:21:41,170 --> 01:21:42,290
It's...

997
01:21:46,540 --> 01:21:48,969
Destructive Death, Leg Type:

998
01:21:48,970 --> 01:21:49,680
Below!

999
01:21:52,180 --> 01:21:54,500
Flying Planet Thousand Wheels!

1000
01:22:00,030 --> 01:22:02,739
Even if I manage to predict his movements
and block his attacks,

1001
01:22:02,740 --> 01:22:05,939
I can't avoid taking damage completely
because the sheer force is too much.

1002
01:22:05,940 --> 01:22:08,029
Every technique is incredibly precise.

1003
01:22:08,030 --> 01:22:11,360
He stabs into openings with unerring accuracy,
like a compass needle.

1004
01:22:14,160 --> 01:22:16,449
Each blow is straight to my vital points,

1005
01:22:16,450 --> 01:22:18,789
like being drawn by a magnet.

1006
01:22:18,790 --> 01:22:20,219
But how?

1007
01:22:20,220 --> 01:22:21,410
What could it be?

1008
01:22:21,920 --> 01:22:24,669
What exactly is it reacting to?

1009
01:22:24,670 --> 01:22:26,710
Remember and think.

1010
01:22:28,090 --> 01:22:29,839
There must be something.

1011
01:22:29,840 --> 01:22:33,220
If I piece together Akaza's actions
and words so far...

1012
01:22:36,600 --> 01:22:39,600
Hinokami Kagura: Solar Heat Haze!

1013
01:22:50,320 --> 01:22:52,569
What an interesting technique.

1014
01:22:52,570 --> 01:22:56,329
The blade I clearly dodged
looked as if it extended.

1015
01:22:56,330 --> 01:22:58,829
How exactly did you swing it?

1016
01:22:58,830 --> 01:23:02,099
The tip of your blade wavered,
like a heat haze.

1017
01:23:02,100 --> 01:23:03,330
How fascinating!

1018
01:23:14,510 --> 01:23:17,600
Hinokami Kagura: Dance!

1019
01:23:20,100 --> 01:23:21,230
This is bad.

1020
01:23:22,190 --> 01:23:23,440
He's gonna break it.

1021
01:23:28,360 --> 01:23:30,280
Good headbutt!

1022
01:23:31,490 --> 01:23:34,240
Let go! Let go of my sword!

1023
01:23:35,620 --> 01:23:39,260
It's no use. He won't let it go.

1024
01:23:51,300 --> 01:23:53,050
Giyu!

1025
01:23:56,640 --> 01:23:59,089
Now I'm pissed off.

1026
01:23:59,090 --> 01:24:01,890
My back hurts like hell.

1027
01:24:02,560 --> 01:24:05,769
You really sent me flying far,

1028
01:24:05,770 --> 01:24:07,710
Upper Rank Three.

1029
01:24:10,610 --> 01:24:15,149
I prefer not to draw my sword
unless absolutely necessary,

1030
01:24:15,150 --> 01:24:19,490
and I don't like sparring with anyone
for amusement.

1031
01:24:20,700 --> 01:24:22,619
But now,

1032
01:24:22,620 --> 01:24:26,079
I've encountered
an overwhelming opponent after so long.

1033
01:24:26,080 --> 01:24:30,000
And in this brief moment,
I can feel my senses sharpening.

1034
01:24:31,320 --> 01:24:34,139
Instincts I had long shut away
are being jolted awake

1035
01:24:34,140 --> 01:24:37,760
and pulled along toward the place
where the strong stand.

1036
01:24:38,470 --> 01:24:41,460
It's how much a life-or-death struggle

1037
01:24:41,970 --> 01:24:45,349
can push one's strength to its limits.

1038
01:24:45,350 --> 01:24:47,010
Now I understand.

1039
01:24:50,610 --> 01:24:52,110
Giyu...

1040
01:25:09,040 --> 01:25:10,709
He manifested the mark?

1041
01:25:10,710 --> 01:25:11,919
His speed...

1042
01:25:11,920 --> 01:25:13,300
...increased!

1043
01:25:17,930 --> 01:25:19,759
Water Breathing, Fourth Form:

1044
01:25:19,760 --> 01:25:21,430
Striking Tide.

1045
01:25:35,570 --> 01:25:37,489
They're both fast.

1046
01:25:37,490 --> 01:25:40,279
Even though Giyu's speed has increased,

1047
01:25:40,280 --> 01:25:42,500
Akaza quickly adapted to it.

1048
01:25:44,740 --> 01:25:47,410
Is that all you've got?!

1049
01:25:56,510 --> 01:25:58,089
More!

1050
01:25:58,090 --> 01:26:00,130
Keep it coming!

1051
01:26:28,960 --> 01:26:32,790
Tenth Form: Constant Flux!

1052
01:26:49,770 --> 01:26:52,939
Seventh Form: Drop Ripple Thrust!

1053
01:26:52,940 --> 01:26:56,230
Destructive Death, Disorder!

1054
01:27:06,780 --> 01:27:09,200
Giyu! Akaza!

1055
01:27:11,160 --> 01:27:12,960
Calm down!

1056
01:27:16,590 --> 01:27:19,089
Think. Don't panic.

1057
01:27:19,090 --> 01:27:21,360
Never stop thinking.

1058
01:27:23,220 --> 01:27:26,850
Why are Akaza's attacks so precise,
like a magnet locking onto its target?

1059
01:27:27,810 --> 01:27:31,770
Why does he always react, even to attacks
from behind or from blind spots?

1060
01:27:32,690 --> 01:27:34,100
Think!

1061
01:27:38,480 --> 01:27:41,149
Your Fighting Spirit is well-developed.

1062
01:27:41,150 --> 01:27:43,610
It's close to the realm of the highest.

1063
01:27:46,780 --> 01:27:48,699
In his fight against Rengoku,

1064
01:27:48,700 --> 01:27:51,910
Akaza mentioned Fighting Spirit.

1065
01:27:53,910 --> 01:27:55,789
What is Fighting Spirit?

1066
01:27:55,790 --> 01:27:58,670
Just like I can sense things
through smell,

1067
01:27:59,250 --> 01:28:01,960
Akaza can sense something
through Fighting Spirit?

1068
01:28:16,100 --> 01:28:20,569
I can feel tingling where
the opponent is about to strike.

1069
01:28:20,570 --> 01:28:24,029
So that's why you noticed
Gyutaro's attack.

1070
01:28:24,030 --> 01:28:26,360
You were amazing,
even though it was from behind.

1071
01:28:28,240 --> 01:28:31,239
My skin's tougher than most humans'.

1072
01:28:31,240 --> 01:28:32,909
Doesn't matter if it's from behind,

1073
01:28:32,910 --> 01:28:36,249
if someone's watching me,
I can feel it.

1074
01:28:36,250 --> 01:28:37,780
Do it and show me!

1075
01:28:38,960 --> 01:28:40,210
Sure!

1076
01:28:45,170 --> 01:28:46,839
You're looking at my right shoulder.

1077
01:28:46,840 --> 01:28:48,590
Wow! You're right.

1078
01:28:49,260 --> 01:28:53,269
Especially the ones staring with killing intent,
I can tell immediately.

1079
01:28:53,270 --> 01:28:56,519
Anything that poses a threat
just hits differently.

1080
01:28:56,520 --> 01:29:00,860
Killing intent is like needles
stabbing into my skin.

1081
01:29:01,690 --> 01:29:05,739
Right, Inosuke could sense things
that couldn't be seen,

1082
01:29:05,740 --> 01:29:08,490
using his finely honed skin.

1083
01:29:09,070 --> 01:29:12,020
After that, what did we talk about?

1084
01:29:12,930 --> 01:29:14,449
That time...

1085
01:29:14,450 --> 01:29:16,119
But on the other hand,

1086
01:29:16,120 --> 01:29:20,959
someone without killing intent
or who's not a threat is hard to notice.

1087
01:29:20,960 --> 01:29:22,960
Like that little old hag!

1088
01:29:23,590 --> 01:29:27,470
That old hag in the house
with the wisteria crest was terrifying.

1089
01:29:28,090 --> 01:29:30,480
Before I even noticed...

1090
01:29:31,850 --> 01:29:35,560
she was sitting behind me,
bringing rice balls.

1091
01:29:36,430 --> 01:29:39,599
Stop calling her hag,
call her madam.

1092
01:29:39,600 --> 01:29:40,519
Madam hag!

1093
01:29:40,520 --> 01:29:41,689
Hey!

1094
01:29:41,690 --> 01:29:43,489
That's what I figured.

1095
01:29:43,490 --> 01:29:46,779
If I can get close without giving off
any killing intent, no one'll notice.

1096
01:29:46,780 --> 01:29:49,700
Then there's no one I can't kill.

1097
01:29:51,950 --> 01:29:57,199
But that's only because she didn't
mean you any harm, right?

1098
01:29:57,200 --> 01:30:01,420
I don't think it's possible to take down
a demon without killing intent.

1099
01:30:03,290 --> 01:30:06,009
Yeah, true enough.

1100
01:30:06,010 --> 01:30:08,799
A half-hearted swing without killing intent

1101
01:30:08,800 --> 01:30:12,100
ain't gonna cut through
a demon's tough neck anyway.

1102
01:30:13,220 --> 01:30:15,429
It was a silly conversation,

1103
01:30:15,430 --> 01:30:18,340
but I feel like there was meaning to it.

1104
01:30:20,350 --> 01:30:23,939
What exactly is this Fighting Spirit
that Akaza senses?

1105
01:30:23,940 --> 01:30:25,819
What is it in his perception?

1106
01:30:25,820 --> 01:30:27,739
Is it different from killing intent?

1107
01:30:27,740 --> 01:30:29,399
Is it the will to fight?

1108
01:30:29,400 --> 01:30:30,859
Time spent in training?

1109
01:30:30,860 --> 01:30:32,270
Or the amount of training?

1110
01:30:33,490 --> 01:30:36,540
Is it something like how
I predict movements through smell?

1111
01:30:38,120 --> 01:30:42,450
Is there any way to throw off
Akaza's fighting compass?

1112
01:30:52,340 --> 01:30:54,640
Hinokami Kagura: Dance!

1113
01:30:57,140 --> 01:30:59,360
You're wide open,

1114
01:30:59,810 --> 01:31:01,350
Tanjiro!

1115
01:31:04,190 --> 01:31:05,460
I'll get hit!

1116
01:31:18,660 --> 01:31:19,829
Fighting Spirit.

1117
01:31:19,830 --> 01:31:21,119
Magnet.

1118
01:31:21,120 --> 01:31:22,580
Compass.

1119
01:31:23,040 --> 01:31:24,289
Sense.

1120
01:31:24,290 --> 01:31:25,329
Killing intent.

1121
01:31:25,330 --> 01:31:26,670
Impossible.

1122
01:31:27,460 --> 01:31:29,380
Realm of the highest.

1123
01:31:30,090 --> 01:31:31,950
I see.

1124
01:31:33,630 --> 01:31:34,880
I remember.

1125
01:31:51,860 --> 01:31:52,399
Hey!

1126
01:31:52,400 --> 01:31:55,279
Father, when you dance
the Hinokami Kagura,

1127
01:31:55,280 --> 01:31:57,200
what are you thinking?

1128
01:31:57,830 --> 01:32:01,830
If it's difficult for you,
I can take your place starting next year.

1129
01:32:02,370 --> 01:32:04,540
I'm worried about your health.

1130
01:32:06,110 --> 01:32:08,669
Thank you, Tanjiro.

1131
01:32:08,670 --> 01:32:14,550
But in the last few years,
I never felt the dance was difficult.

1132
01:32:15,260 --> 01:32:16,929
I know it's strange.

1133
01:32:16,930 --> 01:32:20,559
When I first started learning the Kagura
from your grandfather,

1134
01:32:20,560 --> 01:32:24,559
I was younger, healthier,
and stronger than I am now.

1135
01:32:24,560 --> 01:32:27,900
And yet, I was gasping for breath,
struggling so much back then.

1136
01:32:31,280 --> 01:32:32,859
Once a year,

1137
01:32:32,860 --> 01:32:36,640
at the start of the new year,
the Kamado family performs Kagura,

1138
01:32:37,360 --> 01:32:42,370
a grueling ritual that lasts
from sunset to sunrise for generations.

1139
01:32:43,370 --> 01:32:45,959
All twelve dance forms

1140
01:32:45,960 --> 01:32:50,500
must be repeated hundreds, thousands,
tens of thousands of times until dawn.

1141
01:32:53,420 --> 01:32:57,839
I guess that's because I made
a lot of unnecessary movements.

1142
01:32:57,840 --> 01:33:02,430
What's important is proper breathing
and proper movements.

1143
01:33:03,070 --> 01:33:07,939
It's about exerting the greatest strength
with the smallest movements.

1144
01:33:07,940 --> 01:33:13,410
When you do that,
your head gradually becomes clearer.

1145
01:33:14,800 --> 01:33:16,100
Clear?

1146
01:33:17,070 --> 01:33:18,859
In the beginning,

1147
01:33:18,860 --> 01:33:24,100
you must learn the movements
and sensibilities.

1148
01:33:24,580 --> 01:33:26,289
Open your five senses.

1149
01:33:26,290 --> 01:33:28,209
Become aware of
every part of your body,

1150
01:33:28,210 --> 01:33:31,920
down to each individual blood vessel.

1151
01:33:34,050 --> 01:33:37,049
This part is truly painful.

1152
01:33:37,050 --> 01:33:42,300
You'll feel like no matter how much
you struggle, you can't go further.

1153
01:33:42,810 --> 01:33:46,179
But once you've learned
and absorbed many things,

1154
01:33:46,180 --> 01:33:49,479
the next step is to strip away
what's unnecessary.

1155
01:33:49,480 --> 01:33:53,439
You leave only what's essential
for that movement...

1156
01:33:53,440 --> 01:33:54,670
and then close the rest.

1157
01:33:55,940 --> 01:33:57,360
Close?

1158
01:33:57,900 --> 01:34:00,279
When someone really
wants to listen carefully,

1159
01:34:00,280 --> 01:34:02,490
they often close their eyes, right?

1160
01:34:02,950 --> 01:34:04,369
It's just like that.

1161
01:34:04,370 --> 01:34:09,700
You choose only what's truly
needed at that moment.

1162
01:34:10,210 --> 01:34:15,049
Eventually, you'll be able to open and close
every vein and muscle in your body

1163
01:34:15,050 --> 01:34:19,930
as quickly and effortlessly as blinking.

1164
01:34:21,220 --> 01:34:26,180
And when that happens,
a path bathed in clarity will open.

1165
01:34:28,290 --> 01:34:30,689
When your mind becomes clear,

1166
01:34:30,690 --> 01:34:34,229
you begin to see the Transparent World.

1167
01:34:34,230 --> 01:34:35,869
But that's a realm

1168
01:34:35,870 --> 01:34:41,239
you can only reach through pain, by struggling
with every ounce of your strength.

1169
01:34:41,240 --> 01:34:43,470
Can I go there too?

1170
01:34:44,700 --> 01:34:47,870
If you keep working diligently.

1171
01:34:48,620 --> 01:34:50,709
Here. They're done.

1172
01:34:50,710 --> 01:34:51,900
Thank you.

1173
01:34:55,840 --> 01:34:58,759
Ten days before my father
passed away from illness,

1174
01:34:58,760 --> 01:35:03,280
a bear attacked and ate people
on the next mountain over.

1175
01:35:04,300 --> 01:35:09,600
We lit bonfires around our house
and strung up ropes with bells.

1176
01:35:28,040 --> 01:35:29,620
Tanjiro.

1177
01:35:33,790 --> 01:35:35,290
Yes?

1178
01:35:36,540 --> 01:35:37,920
Come with me.

1179
01:36:26,930 --> 01:36:29,969
I feel sorry because
I know you're hungry.

1180
01:36:29,970 --> 01:36:33,280
But I won't let you come any closer.

1181
01:36:34,430 --> 01:36:40,609
I will show no mercy to anyone
who would harm my family.

1182
01:36:40,610 --> 01:36:43,070
If you ignore my warning,

1183
01:36:46,150 --> 01:36:48,780
I will take your life.

1184
01:37:00,340 --> 01:37:03,959
The bear's head,
which was as thick as a man's body,

1185
01:37:03,960 --> 01:37:07,220
fell to the ground
with the chime of the bells.

1186
01:37:09,050 --> 01:37:11,099
I couldn't follow it with my eyes,

1187
01:37:11,100 --> 01:37:15,940
but I think he struck twice
in the span of a single blink.

1188
01:37:18,100 --> 01:37:19,689
Otherwise,

1189
01:37:19,690 --> 01:37:22,770
it would've been impossible to sever
its head with an axe of that size.

1190
01:37:24,300 --> 01:37:27,070
His scent didn't waver a little.

1191
01:37:27,610 --> 01:37:31,909
Before and after severing the bear's head,
he didn't show fear, didn't flinch,

1192
01:37:31,910 --> 01:37:33,660
and didn't even emit killing intent.

1193
01:37:41,170 --> 01:37:43,010
Did you observe properly?

1194
01:37:44,250 --> 01:37:47,130
Don't forget what you just saw.

1195
01:37:50,050 --> 01:37:53,740
Father wasn't the kind of man
to show off his strength needlessly.

1196
01:37:54,350 --> 01:37:56,100
I realized only later

1197
01:37:56,740 --> 01:38:00,560
that he had given me a lesson.

1198
01:38:01,400 --> 01:38:05,029
So I could learn to see
the Transparent World

1199
01:38:05,030 --> 01:38:06,820
from his movements.

1200
01:38:09,030 --> 01:38:15,740
Grandfather also must have done for him,
and Great-Grandfather before that.

1201
01:38:17,790 --> 01:38:20,419
Never give up.

1202
01:38:20,420 --> 01:38:23,009
Keep thinking.

1203
01:38:23,010 --> 01:38:26,669
So you can eventually
break through any wall

1204
01:38:26,670 --> 01:38:28,740
with unceasing effort.

1205
01:38:30,540 --> 01:38:32,509
I understand, Father.

1206
01:38:32,510 --> 01:38:34,100
That's why, back then,

1207
01:38:34,560 --> 01:38:38,560
I was able to evade that inescapable,
magnetic blow from Akaza.

1208
01:38:41,810 --> 01:38:46,240
That attack would have
probably killed me instantly.

1209
01:38:46,900 --> 01:38:49,609
Giyu and I have been
taking turns attacking,

1210
01:38:49,610 --> 01:38:52,109
giving brief moments
to catch our breath.

1211
01:38:52,110 --> 01:38:55,989
He even shielded me from blows
that could have been fatal.

1212
01:38:55,990 --> 01:38:57,839
But at that moment,

1213
01:38:57,840 --> 01:38:59,950
even he couldn't have made it in time.

1214
01:39:01,120 --> 01:39:02,669
Even so,

1215
01:39:02,670 --> 01:39:06,660
somehow I didn't think
it was impossible.

1216
01:39:07,570 --> 01:39:09,879
I felt it just for a moment.

1217
01:39:09,880 --> 01:39:11,720
That I could enter...

1218
01:39:13,390 --> 01:39:14,720
that world.

1219
01:39:19,100 --> 01:39:21,100
The Transparent World.

1220
01:39:23,690 --> 01:39:26,690
I could see through his body.

1221
01:39:27,980 --> 01:39:31,620
It was the same as
when Hantengu hid his heart.

1222
01:39:32,280 --> 01:39:34,740
I don't know whether
I saw it or smelled it.

1223
01:39:39,840 --> 01:39:41,219
Dodge.

1224
01:39:41,220 --> 01:39:44,170
I closed my other senses
and concentrated on dodging only.

1225
01:39:44,670 --> 01:39:48,380
My body moved faster
than ever before.

1226
01:39:50,170 --> 01:39:53,589
When I entered the Transparent World
that Father taught me about,

1227
01:39:53,590 --> 01:39:56,760
my speed increased drastically
and I could predict his moves faster.

1228
01:39:58,930 --> 01:40:00,929
I could see clearly

1229
01:40:00,930 --> 01:40:03,630
his lungs move and the flow of his blood.

1230
01:40:04,140 --> 01:40:09,360
I got a faster and clearer awareness
of the contraction of my muscles.

1231
01:40:13,240 --> 01:40:17,569
Akaza probably can sense
my Fighting Spirit, but if I close it off,

1232
01:40:17,570 --> 01:40:19,600
I may be able to aim for his head.

1233
01:40:32,630 --> 01:40:34,379
See through it.

1234
01:40:34,380 --> 01:40:35,760
See through it!

1235
01:40:39,140 --> 01:40:42,720
It seems you have already used
all your water techniques.

1236
01:40:43,310 --> 01:40:45,890
That's enough, Giyu.

1237
01:40:46,480 --> 01:40:48,439
Let's end this.

1238
01:40:48,440 --> 01:40:51,360
You did well to make it this far!

1239
01:40:53,030 --> 01:40:54,689
Impossible.

1240
01:40:54,690 --> 01:40:57,030
The blade I swung...

1241
01:40:58,720 --> 01:41:00,450
He hit it from the side...

1242
01:41:02,120 --> 01:41:04,369
and broke it?

1243
01:41:04,370 --> 01:41:05,750
Goodbye.

1244
01:41:35,890 --> 01:41:39,229
He cut off his arm and stopped the attack.

1245
01:41:39,230 --> 01:41:42,850
The sound of his breathing is different,
the look of his hair and eyes too.

1246
01:41:44,200 --> 01:41:46,530
Tanjiro saved me.

1247
01:41:48,130 --> 01:41:50,079
Every cell in my body,

1248
01:41:50,080 --> 01:41:55,120
down to each strand of my hair,
is telling me to kill him right now.

1249
01:41:56,550 --> 01:41:59,680
Something has changed in him.

1250
01:42:00,970 --> 01:42:02,470
He's dangerous.

1251
01:42:04,060 --> 01:42:06,929
He's wary of Tanjiro.

1252
01:42:06,930 --> 01:42:09,060
It's a chance.

1253
01:42:13,440 --> 01:42:16,190
Technique Development, Final Form:

1254
01:42:16,780 --> 01:42:19,070
Blue Silver Chaotic Afterglow!

1255
01:42:22,450 --> 01:42:24,829
The speed of his attacks
is increasing again!

1256
01:42:24,830 --> 01:42:26,660
The power is also increasing!

1257
01:42:27,120 --> 01:42:30,340
Can I block them with Dead Calm?

1258
01:42:52,380 --> 01:42:55,389
So this is what Father
was talking about.

1259
01:42:55,390 --> 01:42:59,180
This is the Transparent World.

1260
01:43:07,620 --> 01:43:09,079
How to say it?

1261
01:43:09,080 --> 01:43:10,609
This is strange.

1262
01:43:10,610 --> 01:43:13,280
Time is moving slowly.

1263
01:43:15,130 --> 01:43:19,650
No, everything looks like
it's moving slowly.

1264
01:43:26,260 --> 01:43:27,839
It was inescapable.

1265
01:43:27,840 --> 01:43:30,730
I got hit with a hundred blows
almost all at once.

1266
01:43:31,760 --> 01:43:35,760
I couldn't block them all
even with Dead Calm.

1267
01:43:37,820 --> 01:43:39,359
How incredible.

1268
01:43:39,360 --> 01:43:41,890
I'm impressed you're still alive.

1269
01:43:42,360 --> 01:43:45,490
Somehow you dodged a fatal blow, I see.

1270
01:43:46,120 --> 01:43:50,119
Don't die like Kyojuro and Tanjiro.

1271
01:43:50,120 --> 01:43:53,100
You should become a demon too, Giyu.

1272
01:43:55,040 --> 01:43:58,510
He hasn't noticed
that Tanjiro is behind him?

1273
01:43:58,960 --> 01:44:01,799
- Did he erase his presence?
- You can't deny that

1274
01:44:01,800 --> 01:44:03,969
- A chance.
- you were happy to have found

1275
01:44:03,970 --> 01:44:05,499
- Tanjiro, take him down!
- an opponent you could

1276
01:44:05,500 --> 01:44:06,219
- Tanjiro, take him down!
- go all out against, right?

1277
01:44:06,220 --> 01:44:08,639
- If you still can move, do it!
- go all out against, right?

1278
01:44:08,640 --> 01:44:12,140
Before he notices you,
aim for his head!

1279
01:44:12,580 --> 01:44:16,020
Akaza!
I'm going to sever your head right now!

1280
01:44:21,860 --> 01:44:24,280
What a fool!
He just called him out!

1281
01:44:24,990 --> 01:44:26,740
He's still alive?

1282
01:44:27,280 --> 01:44:31,449
Even after getting hit
by my last attacks?

1283
01:44:31,450 --> 01:44:33,499
Well, no bother.

1284
01:44:33,500 --> 01:44:34,959
No matter the attack,

1285
01:44:34,960 --> 01:44:38,339
my Destructive Death Compass
Needle will detect it.

1286
01:44:38,340 --> 01:44:44,300
The stronger my opponent's Fighting Spirit,
the stronger my Compass Needle reacts.

1287
01:44:47,970 --> 01:44:49,430
What?

1288
01:44:49,930 --> 01:44:52,810
What is this odd presence?

1289
01:44:53,270 --> 01:44:57,710
It's like he has become
a different creature.

1290
01:44:59,060 --> 01:45:01,069
His Fighting Spirit is gone?

1291
01:45:01,070 --> 01:45:02,779
He has no Fighting Spirit!

1292
01:45:02,780 --> 01:45:04,819
Calm down!

1293
01:45:04,820 --> 01:45:05,800
He's coming!

1294
01:45:12,160 --> 01:45:16,160
Hinokami Kagura:
Setting Sun Transformation.

1295
01:45:38,140 --> 01:45:41,190
No way...

1296
01:45:47,990 --> 01:45:50,159
I've never seen a human

1297
01:45:50,160 --> 01:45:53,760
without Fighting Spirit
in the last few hundred years.

1298
01:45:54,370 --> 01:46:00,209
Even a baby has a faint
Fighting Spirit, but he...

1299
01:46:00,210 --> 01:46:04,550
His Fighting Spirit completely
disappeared at that moment.

1300
01:46:08,380 --> 01:46:12,799
As if I were face-to-face
with something that shouldn't exist.

1301
01:46:12,800 --> 01:46:15,599
My senses were thrown into confusion.

1302
01:46:15,600 --> 01:46:18,310
My compass didn't react.

1303
01:46:20,690 --> 01:46:23,609
But that's not the problem.

1304
01:46:23,610 --> 01:46:25,339
In battle,

1305
01:46:25,340 --> 01:46:28,569
you must immediately
understand and respond to

1306
01:46:28,570 --> 01:46:32,659
every unexpected situation
you encounter for the first time.

1307
01:46:32,660 --> 01:46:34,870
I can do that.

1308
01:46:36,160 --> 01:46:38,500
Or so I thought...

1309
01:46:39,460 --> 01:46:42,709
However, in this brief battle,

1310
01:46:42,710 --> 01:46:46,770
he grasped something
and surpassed my speed.

1311
01:46:47,340 --> 01:46:49,719
The culmination of centuries
of martial arts

1312
01:46:49,720 --> 01:46:54,100
was shattered head-on,
fair and square.

1313
01:46:54,760 --> 01:46:59,479
There was no hatred
or anger in his eyes.

1314
01:46:59,480 --> 01:47:02,270
No killing intent or Fighting Spirit.

1315
01:47:02,850 --> 01:47:06,189
Perhaps what his eyes perceived was

1316
01:47:06,190 --> 01:47:10,240
the realm of the highest
I've been seeking.

1317
01:47:11,820 --> 01:47:14,370
Nothing less than a Selfless State.

1318
01:47:16,450 --> 01:47:21,210
I had vaguely sensed that
such a state existed,

1319
01:47:21,830 --> 01:47:25,960
but even now,
I still haven't been able to reach it.

1320
01:47:35,300 --> 01:47:36,799
Not yet!

1321
01:47:36,800 --> 01:47:38,889
I can still fight!

1322
01:47:38,890 --> 01:47:41,810
I can still get stronger!

1323
01:47:47,650 --> 01:47:50,740
He's trying to connect his head back?

1324
01:47:59,830 --> 01:48:01,580
I can't die...

1325
01:48:03,620 --> 01:48:05,710
in this place.

1326
01:48:08,290 --> 01:48:10,510
I will get stronger!

1327
01:48:13,300 --> 01:48:16,220
I must become stronger than anyone!

1328
01:48:16,640 --> 01:48:18,390
Stronger!

1329
01:48:20,640 --> 01:48:24,020
And even stronger!

1330
01:48:33,320 --> 01:48:34,989
His head's vanished.

1331
01:48:34,990 --> 01:48:36,410
It's over.

1332
01:48:37,950 --> 01:48:39,580
We won.

1333
01:48:44,500 --> 01:48:46,190
I'm dizzy.

1334
01:48:47,830 --> 01:48:50,129
My muscles are twitching...

1335
01:48:50,130 --> 01:48:52,380
My body's already at its limit.

1336
01:48:54,760 --> 01:48:56,550
Are you all right, Tanji—

1337
01:48:58,340 --> 01:49:01,119
His body isn't disintegrating.

1338
01:49:01,120 --> 01:49:03,850
Oh no, this is bad.

1339
01:49:04,270 --> 01:49:04,810
Tan—

1340
01:49:16,400 --> 01:49:19,449
He still can move.
His body hasn't vanished.

1341
01:49:19,450 --> 01:49:21,870
The wound on the neck is closing up.

1342
01:49:24,870 --> 01:49:26,790
My head is spinning.

1343
01:49:39,340 --> 01:49:42,099
No way! Impossible!

1344
01:49:42,100 --> 01:49:44,180
He didn't die after I severed his head.

1345
01:49:44,600 --> 01:49:46,389
Is there some kind of condition?

1346
01:49:46,390 --> 01:49:48,519
Like with Gyutaro and Daki?

1347
01:49:48,520 --> 01:49:49,599
No, that's not it.

1348
01:49:49,600 --> 01:49:51,939
I see his head's vanished.

1349
01:49:51,940 --> 01:49:54,109
He's changing.

1350
01:49:54,110 --> 01:49:56,780
Akaza is turning into something else.

1351
01:50:03,740 --> 01:50:08,080
He's becoming like Muzan.
The head is no longer his weakness.

1352
01:50:08,750 --> 01:50:10,789
The fight isn't over.

1353
01:50:10,790 --> 01:50:12,960
The fight...

1354
01:50:13,500 --> 01:50:14,669
Tanjiro!

1355
01:50:14,670 --> 01:50:16,459
He fainted?

1356
01:50:16,460 --> 01:50:17,919
Of course.

1357
01:50:17,920 --> 01:50:20,260
He's already gone
way past his limit.

1358
01:50:30,100 --> 01:50:33,360
Water Breathing, Fourth Form:

1359
01:50:35,820 --> 01:50:37,400
Striking Tide!

1360
01:50:42,160 --> 01:50:44,099
He's regenerating?

1361
01:50:44,100 --> 01:50:47,290
He's regenerating so quickly
despite losing his head!

1362
01:51:11,390 --> 01:51:16,190
I can't hear anything in my left ear.
I can't feel my right hand.

1363
01:51:17,400 --> 01:51:20,900
I still have strength, but for how long?

1364
01:51:29,790 --> 01:51:31,330
Wait!

1365
01:51:31,750 --> 01:51:36,420
I am... still alive.

1366
01:51:37,300 --> 01:51:41,800
If you want to kill Tanjiro,
defeat me first!

1367
01:51:45,890 --> 01:51:48,219
An unbreakable spirit.

1368
01:51:48,220 --> 01:51:52,810
No matter how dire the situation,
it never breaks.

1369
01:51:53,440 --> 01:51:56,269
We are not samurai.

1370
01:51:56,270 --> 01:51:58,269
We do not carry a sword.

1371
01:51:58,270 --> 01:52:01,780
But we have swords in our hearts.

1372
01:52:03,030 --> 01:52:05,950
But we have swords in our hearts.

1373
01:52:07,070 --> 01:52:10,750
We only use our fists.

1374
01:52:12,290 --> 01:52:15,500
What a nuisance.

1375
01:52:26,010 --> 01:52:27,390
Stop it.

1376
01:52:33,640 --> 01:52:35,060
Who?

1377
01:52:40,860 --> 01:52:44,570
Hakuji, please stop.

1378
01:52:47,620 --> 01:52:49,369
Let go.

1379
01:52:49,370 --> 01:52:51,240
Let go of my hand!

1380
01:52:51,790 --> 01:52:53,960
Who are you?

1381
01:52:55,710 --> 01:52:58,220
That's enough.

1382
01:52:58,960 --> 01:53:01,170
Let's go to the other side.

1383
01:53:01,920 --> 01:53:07,180
No. I must kill them.

1384
01:53:08,550 --> 01:53:10,560
Why?

1385
01:53:11,140 --> 01:53:14,560
I must get stronger.

1386
01:53:15,090 --> 01:53:17,760
I'll kill anyone who gets in my way.

1387
01:53:19,060 --> 01:53:20,940
But why?

1388
01:53:21,690 --> 01:53:24,690
Why do you want to be strong?

1389
01:53:26,400 --> 01:53:27,990
Because...

1390
01:53:28,610 --> 01:53:33,870
If I'm not strong,
I can't bring back...

1391
01:53:36,160 --> 01:53:38,620
medicine for my father.

1392
01:53:40,500 --> 01:53:42,840
If I don't get stronger,

1393
01:53:45,010 --> 01:53:48,930
I can't steal someone's wallet
and get away.

1394
01:53:50,180 --> 01:53:54,930
If I don't get stronger,
I can't win when they retaliate.

1395
01:53:55,730 --> 01:53:57,809
If I don't get stronger,

1396
01:53:57,810 --> 01:54:01,340
the Magistrate will catch me
and punish me.

1397
01:54:04,730 --> 01:54:08,820
You already have three lines
of pickpockets' tattoos on each arm.

1398
01:54:09,280 --> 01:54:11,620
Do it again, and we'll cut off your hands.

1399
01:54:19,620 --> 01:54:21,829
Get down, you brat!

1400
01:54:21,830 --> 01:54:24,089
If you're gonna do it, then do it!

1401
01:54:24,090 --> 01:54:26,879
If you cut off my hands,
I still have my feet!

1402
01:54:26,880 --> 01:54:29,259
I'll pick pockets with my feet!

1403
01:54:29,260 --> 01:54:32,220
I won't let you catch me next time!

1404
01:54:34,760 --> 01:54:38,349
At just eleven years old,
repeatedly committed crimes,

1405
01:54:38,350 --> 01:54:42,059
endured a hundred-beating
that can make even grown men faint,

1406
01:54:42,060 --> 01:54:43,770
and yet remains defiant.

1407
01:54:44,650 --> 01:54:46,569
You are a demon child!

1408
01:54:46,570 --> 01:54:48,689
Say whatever you want!

1409
01:54:48,690 --> 01:54:51,359
You're right. I am a demon child.

1410
01:54:51,360 --> 01:54:54,829
They say I had teeth
from the moment I was born.

1411
01:54:54,830 --> 01:54:55,529
Insolent!

1412
01:54:55,530 --> 01:54:56,869
You brat!

1413
01:54:56,870 --> 01:54:59,810
I don't care if I'm a demon child!
You bastard!

1414
01:55:00,960 --> 01:55:08,510
MINAMI-MACHI MAGISTRATE'S OFFICE

1415
01:55:09,420 --> 01:55:13,179
Hakuji!

1416
01:55:13,180 --> 01:55:15,389
When he heard you got arrested again,

1417
01:55:15,390 --> 01:55:18,750
your father hanged himself,
and he's dead!

1418
01:55:19,390 --> 01:55:21,840
He's dead!

1419
01:55:26,820 --> 01:55:28,730
Dear Hakuji.

1420
01:55:29,860 --> 01:55:32,070
Live a proper life.

1421
01:55:32,610 --> 01:55:34,740
You can still start over.

1422
01:55:42,000 --> 01:55:47,210
Are the poor not even allowed to live?

1423
01:55:52,220 --> 01:55:53,680
Father...

1424
01:55:55,970 --> 01:55:59,640
Screw this world.

1425
01:56:02,730 --> 01:56:06,730
To hell with every last one of them.

1426
01:56:10,570 --> 01:56:13,949
Why do these rotten people get to live,

1427
01:56:13,950 --> 01:56:17,410
but my father had to die?!

1428
01:56:17,860 --> 01:56:20,119
He wasn't a bother.

1429
01:56:20,120 --> 01:56:22,409
Why did he have to apologize?

1430
01:56:22,410 --> 01:56:25,540
My father didn't do anything wrong.

1431
01:56:28,040 --> 01:56:30,499
I could even take the punishment
for stealing.

1432
01:56:30,500 --> 01:56:32,299
It didn't hurt me.

1433
01:56:32,300 --> 01:56:34,259
Even if I'm whipped mercilessly...

1434
01:56:34,260 --> 01:56:36,179
Even if I have my bones broken...

1435
01:56:36,180 --> 01:56:38,179
I can endure it for my father.

1436
01:56:38,180 --> 01:56:39,509
Even for hundreds of years.

1437
01:56:39,510 --> 01:56:42,310
Repent! Do honest work!

1438
01:56:42,890 --> 01:56:45,939
Shut up, you bastard!

1439
01:56:45,940 --> 01:56:48,109
I don't have enough money.

1440
01:56:48,110 --> 01:56:50,800
Medicine is expensive, you know.

1441
01:56:52,150 --> 01:56:55,650
My dad kept getting thinner.

1442
01:56:56,950 --> 01:57:00,449
The bones were beginning
to show through his back.

1443
01:57:00,450 --> 01:57:03,700
I just wanted to feed him
something more nutritious.

1444
01:57:05,960 --> 01:57:08,460
I would've been happy to die instead.

1445
01:57:10,920 --> 01:57:13,090
If it were for my father's sake.

1446
01:57:19,260 --> 01:57:23,140
If it were for my father's sake!

1447
01:57:31,230 --> 01:57:34,569
You're pretty good.

1448
01:57:34,570 --> 01:57:38,159
I was called in because
a kid was about to be killed,

1449
01:57:38,160 --> 01:57:41,520
but you already knocked out
seven adults with your bare hands.

1450
01:57:42,080 --> 01:57:44,579
You've got talent.

1451
01:57:44,580 --> 01:57:48,209
Beating adults without even
picking up a weapon.

1452
01:57:48,210 --> 01:57:50,880
You're one impressive guy.

1453
01:57:52,880 --> 01:57:55,259
Who is this guy?

1454
01:57:55,260 --> 01:57:57,720
What am I seeing?

1455
01:57:58,300 --> 01:58:00,679
Are these my memories?

1456
01:58:00,680 --> 01:58:02,759
Wanna come to my dojo?

1457
01:58:02,760 --> 01:58:05,389
I don't have a single disciple.

1458
01:58:05,390 --> 01:58:07,139
Shut up, old man!

1459
01:58:07,140 --> 01:58:08,639
I'll kill you!

1460
01:58:08,640 --> 01:58:10,140
Those tattoos...

1461
01:58:10,730 --> 01:58:12,979
A criminal from Edo, eh?

1462
01:58:12,980 --> 01:58:17,699
So you were banished from Edo
and ended up in this place?

1463
01:58:17,700 --> 01:58:19,819
What if I did?

1464
01:58:19,820 --> 01:58:22,320
It's got nothing to do with you!

1465
01:58:23,330 --> 01:58:25,940
First, start over, boy.

1466
01:58:26,700 --> 01:58:28,290
So come on!

1467
01:58:29,040 --> 01:58:30,289
You...

1468
01:58:30,290 --> 01:58:33,210
Drop dead, old man!

1469
01:58:51,230 --> 01:58:52,439
SORYU DOJO

1470
01:58:52,440 --> 01:58:55,609
SORYU DOJO
You're really tough.

1471
01:58:55,610 --> 01:58:57,399
Even after all that beating,

1472
01:58:57,400 --> 01:58:59,950
you woke up in less than an hour.

1473
01:59:00,450 --> 01:59:02,319
I'm Keizo.

1474
01:59:02,320 --> 01:59:06,989
I run a dojo for a martial art called Soryu,
which is hand-to-hand combat,

1475
01:59:06,990 --> 01:59:10,140
but I don't have a single disciple.

1476
01:59:10,620 --> 01:59:14,460
So I make a living doing odd jobs.

1477
01:59:16,920 --> 01:59:22,509
The first thing I want you to do
is take care of my sick daughter.

1478
01:59:22,510 --> 01:59:25,550
I leave her to you because
I have some work to do.

1479
01:59:26,470 --> 01:59:31,140
The other day, my wife was exhausted
from nursing and drowned herself.

1480
01:59:32,230 --> 01:59:34,360
Life is hard.

1481
01:59:38,190 --> 01:59:41,109
Truly, because of how pathetic I am,

1482
01:59:41,110 --> 01:59:43,740
I've caused both my wife
and daughter so much hardship.

1483
01:59:46,280 --> 01:59:48,489
You sure want to have me, a criminal,

1484
01:59:48,490 --> 01:59:51,440
nurse your daughter alone?

1485
01:59:53,170 --> 01:59:57,379
I already beat up
that criminal a while ago,

1486
01:59:57,380 --> 01:59:59,250
so it's fine now.

1487
02:00:01,880 --> 02:00:04,030
They are similar.

1488
02:00:11,310 --> 02:00:13,060
I see.

1489
02:00:14,770 --> 02:00:18,149
The reason I found you
so unpleasant

1490
02:00:18,150 --> 02:00:22,490
was that you reminded me
of such a worthless past.

1491
02:00:27,320 --> 02:00:29,910
This is my daughter Koyuki.

1492
02:00:32,660 --> 02:00:34,860
What a ridiculous past.

1493
02:00:38,460 --> 02:00:40,630
Ridiculous...

1494
02:00:48,970 --> 02:00:52,520
Hakuji, forgive me.

1495
02:00:54,060 --> 02:00:55,640
How are you feeling, Koyuki?

1496
02:00:57,810 --> 02:00:59,440
Are you okay to get up?

1497
02:01:02,190 --> 02:01:05,630
You're looking better
than this morning.

1498
02:01:06,160 --> 02:01:07,490
Feeling well, I guess.

1499
02:01:11,330 --> 02:01:12,909
So he's...

1500
02:01:12,910 --> 02:01:14,330
His name...

1501
02:01:15,330 --> 02:01:18,249
Well, he won't tell me his name.

1502
02:01:18,250 --> 02:01:20,670
Hey, don't just stand there.

1503
02:01:21,880 --> 02:01:23,300
Sit here.

1504
02:01:25,170 --> 02:01:28,220
Then, try to get his name
before I get back.

1505
02:01:39,560 --> 02:01:40,900
Umm...

1506
02:01:43,070 --> 02:01:48,530
Your face... Do those wounds hurt?

1507
02:01:51,740 --> 02:01:53,869
It will get better.

1508
02:01:53,870 --> 02:01:56,750
Save... Protect...

1509
02:01:57,620 --> 02:02:02,419
My life was nothing
but a worthless mess of

1510
02:02:02,420 --> 02:02:04,760
delusional ranting.

1511
02:02:21,060 --> 02:02:22,860
Thank you.

1512
02:02:24,270 --> 02:02:26,819
No need to thank me every time.

1513
02:02:26,820 --> 02:02:29,030
Please just go back to sleep.

1514
02:02:30,490 --> 02:02:34,449
Sorry for being a bother.

1515
02:02:34,450 --> 02:02:36,540
I said it's fine.

1516
02:02:38,330 --> 02:02:41,000
Should I close it?

1517
02:02:43,210 --> 02:02:45,250
Leave it be.

1518
02:02:47,380 --> 02:02:50,510
Koyuki was really frail.

1519
02:02:51,550 --> 02:02:53,889
I had to stay by her side all night,

1520
02:02:53,890 --> 02:02:57,679
changing the towel on her forehead,
helping her change the bedding,

1521
02:02:57,680 --> 02:03:00,099
giving her water regularly,

1522
02:03:00,100 --> 02:03:01,689
and of course,

1523
02:03:01,690 --> 02:03:05,070
carrying her whenever
she needed to go to the privy.

1524
02:03:08,280 --> 02:03:12,409
I always nursed my father.

1525
02:03:12,410 --> 02:03:15,909
I could endure more than
the average person,

1526
02:03:15,910 --> 02:03:18,000
so it wasn't all that hard.

1527
02:03:22,670 --> 02:03:25,040
Sorry for everything.

1528
02:03:32,010 --> 02:03:37,140
Why do people suffering from illness
always apologize?

1529
02:03:37,850 --> 02:03:40,599
Apologizing for being a burden.

1530
02:03:40,600 --> 02:03:43,919
Apologizing for their noisy coughing.

1531
02:03:43,920 --> 02:03:47,400
Apologizing because
they can't work properly.

1532
02:03:49,230 --> 02:03:52,239
They'd want to take care
of themselves if they could.

1533
02:03:52,240 --> 02:03:54,359
When they can't stop coughing,

1534
02:03:54,360 --> 02:03:57,200
I bet they want to breathe normally.

1535
02:03:57,870 --> 02:04:02,290
They're the ones suffering the most.

1536
02:04:05,000 --> 02:04:07,629
Sorry for everything.

1537
02:04:07,630 --> 02:04:12,259
Because of me, you can't go training

1538
02:04:12,260 --> 02:04:14,540
or have fun.

1539
02:04:15,470 --> 02:04:19,639
I never think about having fun.

1540
02:04:19,640 --> 02:04:22,599
And I train around here in my free time.

1541
02:04:22,600 --> 02:04:24,140
So pay no mind.

1542
02:04:25,580 --> 02:04:31,149
But sometimes you need a break.

1543
02:04:31,150 --> 02:04:36,580
I hear there will be fireworks tonight,
so you should go.

1544
02:04:37,910 --> 02:04:39,829
How about this?

1545
02:04:39,830 --> 02:04:42,199
Once your dizziness settles down,

1546
02:04:42,200 --> 02:04:45,340
shall I carry you on my back
to the foot of the bridge?

1547
02:04:50,590 --> 02:04:52,629
Even if you can't go today,

1548
02:04:52,630 --> 02:04:55,799
there will be fireworks next year
and the year after that.

1549
02:04:55,800 --> 02:04:58,180
You can go then.

1550
02:05:06,690 --> 02:05:10,569
The only thing I found troublesome
about nursing her

1551
02:05:10,570 --> 02:05:15,780
was how Koyuki would suddenly start
sobbing in the middle of a conversation.

1552
02:05:16,410 --> 02:05:19,409
She was probably feeling down
from being stuck in bed,

1553
02:05:19,410 --> 02:05:22,870
but when she cried, I felt really bad.

1554
02:05:24,580 --> 02:05:27,080
SORYU

1555
02:05:38,260 --> 02:05:40,349
Oh, I see.

1556
02:05:40,350 --> 02:05:42,539
The "Haku" in Hakuji is this one.

1557
02:05:42,540 --> 02:05:44,579
The same character as "Koma" in komainu.

1558
02:05:44,580 --> 02:05:46,059
I get it now.

1559
02:05:46,060 --> 02:05:48,689
I knew it, you're the same as me.

1560
02:05:48,690 --> 02:05:51,899
You need to have something to protect.

1561
02:05:51,900 --> 02:05:55,360
Like a komainu protecting a shrine.

1562
02:06:00,700 --> 02:06:03,489
The reason my master,
who wasn't even a samurai,

1563
02:06:03,490 --> 02:06:07,159
owns such a large piece of land
and a dojo is apparently

1564
02:06:07,160 --> 02:06:11,039
because he saved an old man
who was being attacked by bandits.

1565
02:06:11,040 --> 02:06:14,709
That old man was deeply moved
by the Soryu style.

1566
02:06:14,710 --> 02:06:20,020
And since he had no heir, he gave his land
and the old dojo to my master.

1567
02:06:22,970 --> 02:06:24,259
However,

1568
02:06:24,260 --> 02:06:27,619
there were others who wanted
the land for themselves.

1569
02:06:27,620 --> 02:06:29,689
They weren't pleased.

1570
02:06:29,690 --> 02:06:35,070
The neighboring swordsmanship dojo
was harassing the Soryu dojo.

1571
02:06:36,570 --> 02:06:41,490
Because of that, the Soryu dojo
didn't gain any new disciples.

1572
02:06:48,620 --> 02:06:53,130
But through training here
and nursing Koyuki,

1573
02:06:54,750 --> 02:06:58,050
my heart was saved.

1574
02:07:17,150 --> 02:07:21,240
Three years passed,
and I turned eighteen.

1575
02:07:22,160 --> 02:07:24,119
Koyuki turned sixteen.

1576
02:07:24,120 --> 02:07:26,619
She almost stopped being bedridden

1577
02:07:26,620 --> 02:07:29,500
and was able to live
a normal life again.

1578
02:07:33,750 --> 02:07:35,920
Hakuji, come here.

1579
02:07:36,670 --> 02:07:37,730
Yes.

1580
02:07:39,460 --> 02:07:40,969
Here's the thing.

1581
02:07:40,970 --> 02:07:44,290
Will you inherit this dojo for me, Hakuji?

1582
02:07:44,800 --> 02:07:48,220
Koyuki said she likes you too.

1583
02:07:57,820 --> 02:08:01,819
I had been branded as a criminal,

1584
02:08:01,820 --> 02:08:04,370
so I couldn't really picture my future.

1585
02:08:05,950 --> 02:08:07,409
Let alone a future

1586
02:08:07,410 --> 02:08:12,330
where someone might actually like me.

1587
02:08:14,290 --> 02:08:18,499
But maybe, like my father said,

1588
02:08:18,500 --> 02:08:21,840
I could start living a proper life
from here on out?

1589
02:08:23,090 --> 02:08:27,639
A faint hope to start over
began swelling inside me,

1590
02:08:27,640 --> 02:08:31,180
so much that I couldn't contain it.

1591
02:08:37,480 --> 02:08:39,769
At that time,

1592
02:08:39,770 --> 02:08:45,060
I never even dreamed that the two people
I wanted to protect with my life

1593
02:08:45,570 --> 02:08:48,120
would be poisoned.

1594
02:08:53,120 --> 02:08:56,540
I went to visit my father's grave.

1595
02:08:57,170 --> 02:09:00,340
I told him that I would get married.

1596
02:09:09,850 --> 02:09:13,350
I returned to the dojo
before nightfall, but...

1597
02:09:16,980 --> 02:09:19,690
I felt like throwing up
even before hearing anything.

1598
02:09:20,650 --> 02:09:23,149
My diaphragm was twitching,

1599
02:09:23,150 --> 02:09:26,490
and a bad feeling sent chills
down my spine.

1600
02:09:28,780 --> 02:09:31,280
Someone put poison in the well!

1601
02:09:32,160 --> 02:09:35,579
Because they couldn't beat
Keizo or you in a fair fight,

1602
02:09:35,580 --> 02:09:37,919
they did something cruel!

1603
02:09:37,920 --> 02:09:40,539
So atrocious, this is too much!

1604
02:09:40,540 --> 02:09:42,880
Even Koyuki was killed!

1605
02:09:45,670 --> 02:09:51,049
Whenever the people most important
to me were in danger,

1606
02:09:51,050 --> 02:09:53,310
I was never by their side.

1607
02:10:02,230 --> 02:10:05,470
Even though I had promised.

1608
02:10:07,490 --> 02:10:09,990
Are you fine with me?

1609
02:10:12,240 --> 02:10:16,709
When we were kids,
you told me we would see fireworks.

1610
02:10:16,710 --> 02:10:18,540
Do you remember?

1611
02:10:20,250 --> 02:10:23,420
Well, uh...

1612
02:10:24,750 --> 02:10:27,839
The little conversations
I had with you

1613
02:10:27,840 --> 02:10:32,220
brought me so much happiness.

1614
02:10:33,680 --> 02:10:37,139
Even though I couldn't
see fireworks that year,

1615
02:10:37,140 --> 02:10:42,230
you said I could go next year
and the year after that.

1616
02:10:43,110 --> 02:10:51,450
I couldn't imagine living another year
or the year after that.

1617
02:10:52,740 --> 02:10:54,690
My mother was the same.

1618
02:10:55,200 --> 02:10:59,119
She didn't want to see me die,

1619
02:10:59,120 --> 02:11:02,499
so she killed herself, I think.

1620
02:11:02,500 --> 02:11:07,760
Also, I could tell that my father
had given up somewhere in his heart.

1621
02:11:08,630 --> 02:11:11,340
Because I was far too frail.

1622
02:11:12,390 --> 02:11:17,720
But you could see my future.

1623
02:11:18,560 --> 02:11:20,979
As if it were just a matter of fact.

1624
02:11:20,980 --> 02:11:25,070
You talked to me about next year
and the year after that.

1625
02:11:25,940 --> 02:11:28,440
I was very happy.

1626
02:11:39,790 --> 02:11:42,710
Yes, I am fine with you.

1627
02:11:44,630 --> 02:11:49,210
Will you become my husband?

1628
02:11:57,180 --> 02:11:58,130
Yes.

1629
02:11:58,850 --> 02:12:01,520
I will get stronger than anyone

1630
02:12:01,940 --> 02:12:04,370
and protect you for life.

1631
02:12:08,900 --> 02:12:13,109
In the end, it was all talk.

1632
02:12:13,110 --> 02:12:16,240
I wasn't able to accomplish
a single thing.

1633
02:12:28,670 --> 02:12:30,340
Who are you?

1634
02:12:31,700 --> 02:12:33,469
That's rude!

1635
02:12:33,470 --> 02:12:35,950
You're from Soryu...

1636
02:12:59,740 --> 02:13:02,829
After the father and daughter
of the Soryu dojo were poisoned,

1637
02:13:02,830 --> 02:13:07,919
the single surviving disciple attacked
the neighboring swordsmanship dojo

1638
02:13:07,920 --> 02:13:10,799
and killed sixty-seven people.

1639
02:13:10,800 --> 02:13:14,799
Crushing their skulls and destroying
internal organs with his bare hands.

1640
02:13:14,800 --> 02:13:16,629
Most of the bodies were

1641
02:13:16,630 --> 02:13:19,639
so mangled and deformed,
they were unrecognizable,

1642
02:13:19,640 --> 02:13:22,559
with large portions
of their bodies missing.

1643
02:13:22,560 --> 02:13:26,979
Jaws, brains, eyeballs, limbs,
and innards splattered,

1644
02:13:26,980 --> 02:13:29,229
stuck to the ceiling and walls.

1645
02:13:29,230 --> 02:13:30,859
It was a hellish sight.

1646
02:13:30,860 --> 02:13:33,820
The perpetrator is no ordinary human.

1647
02:13:57,340 --> 02:14:01,259
There was a huge commotion
about a demon appearing in

1648
02:14:01,260 --> 02:14:04,319
a place where I don't remember
assigning demons.

1649
02:14:04,320 --> 02:14:07,439
After I went out of my way
to come here,

1650
02:14:07,440 --> 02:14:10,099
turns out it was just a mere human.

1651
02:14:10,100 --> 02:14:12,440
How boring.

1652
02:14:13,440 --> 02:14:14,780
Move.

1653
02:14:15,440 --> 02:14:16,240
I'll kill you.

1654
02:14:21,410 --> 02:14:26,350
I'm thinking about making
twelve powerful demons.

1655
02:14:27,080 --> 02:14:31,790
Can you withstand the amount
of blood I'm giving you?

1656
02:14:33,750 --> 02:14:39,009
No... thing...

1657
02:14:39,010 --> 02:14:44,600
Nothing matters... to me anymore.

1658
02:14:59,610 --> 02:15:02,739
I turned into a demon,
lost my memories,

1659
02:15:02,740 --> 02:15:05,790
and began seeking strength again.

1660
02:15:21,260 --> 02:15:22,639
More!

1661
02:15:22,640 --> 02:15:24,890
Keep it coming!

1662
02:15:28,730 --> 02:15:35,360
There was nothing left of
what I wanted to protect.

1663
02:15:37,820 --> 02:15:44,700
I didn't even truly wish to go on
living in a world without my family.

1664
02:15:47,410 --> 02:15:52,460
And yet, for over a hundred years,
I kept on killing for no reason.

1665
02:15:53,500 --> 02:15:58,210
What a pitiful, pathetic,

1666
02:15:59,550 --> 02:16:02,050
meaningless story.

1667
02:16:07,430 --> 02:16:09,469
Even if I die,

1668
02:16:09,470 --> 02:16:12,850
I can't go to the same place as them.

1669
02:16:14,310 --> 02:16:19,360
How dare you make me
remember that past.

1670
02:16:21,110 --> 02:16:23,319
Humans...

1671
02:16:23,320 --> 02:16:26,370
Just a soft, fragile, weak creature.

1672
02:16:27,240 --> 02:16:33,670
They die easily.
They break. They disappear.

1673
02:16:36,750 --> 02:16:38,669
He's not dead yet?

1674
02:16:38,670 --> 02:16:40,590
That's absurd!

1675
02:16:41,820 --> 02:16:44,290
I have to finish him now.

1676
02:16:45,490 --> 02:16:49,430
If he regenerated now,
there's no next time.

1677
02:16:55,690 --> 02:16:58,480
I fainted during a fight.

1678
02:17:00,230 --> 02:17:01,729
His head...

1679
02:17:01,730 --> 02:17:04,150
His head is regenerating.

1680
02:17:05,700 --> 02:17:07,730
Even though I severed it earlier.

1681
02:17:13,620 --> 02:17:16,330
Destructive Death, Annihilation Type.

1682
02:17:17,210 --> 02:17:19,209
Stop!

1683
02:17:19,210 --> 02:17:22,169
He still can move?!

1684
02:17:22,170 --> 02:17:24,379
I'll sever his head,
no matter how many times,

1685
02:17:24,380 --> 02:17:25,379
and win this.

1686
02:17:25,380 --> 02:17:28,110
Giyu and I are going to beat Akaza.

1687
02:17:31,600 --> 02:17:33,220
My sword...

1688
02:17:34,520 --> 02:17:36,850
It slipped out.

1689
02:17:37,850 --> 02:17:39,480
I lost my grip.

1690
02:17:48,450 --> 02:17:50,020
Start over...

1691
02:17:51,330 --> 02:17:52,500
Boy.

1692
02:17:55,330 --> 02:17:58,000
I hate the weak.

1693
02:17:59,790 --> 02:18:04,549
The weak don't fight fair.

1694
02:18:04,550 --> 02:18:06,700
They poison the well instead.

1695
02:18:07,430 --> 02:18:09,140
It's disgusting.

1696
02:18:10,300 --> 02:18:16,980
The weak lack patience and fall into
despair at the first sign of struggle.

1697
02:18:18,730 --> 02:18:21,690
I killed people with hands
meant to protect.

1698
02:18:23,320 --> 02:18:27,070
I stained Master's precious
Soryu style in blood.

1699
02:18:28,030 --> 02:18:30,700
I couldn't even uphold
my father's last wish.

1700
02:18:33,580 --> 02:18:38,000
Right, the one I wanted to kill was...

1701
02:18:43,550 --> 02:18:44,959
Oh no, this is bad!

1702
02:18:44,960 --> 02:18:46,710
My sword went flying.

1703
02:18:48,420 --> 02:18:50,590
Punches won't stop him.

1704
02:19:01,190 --> 02:19:05,530
Akaza is trying to use the Annihilation Type
he used against Rengoku.

1705
02:19:08,610 --> 02:19:12,080
I'll take Giyu outside the attack range.

1706
02:19:16,540 --> 02:19:18,700
Don't mind me!

1707
02:19:24,110 --> 02:19:26,100
I must kill...

1708
02:19:28,590 --> 02:19:33,060
the weak I despise!

1709
02:20:15,970 --> 02:20:18,720
He did it to himself.

1710
02:20:21,260 --> 02:20:23,770
Why did he attack himself?

1711
02:20:24,310 --> 02:20:25,770
Why?

1712
02:20:28,940 --> 02:20:30,240
For a moment,

1713
02:20:30,780 --> 02:20:33,250
I smelled the scent
of gratitude from Akaza.

1714
02:20:34,530 --> 02:20:36,530
Why did he smile?

1715
02:20:40,790 --> 02:20:43,329
That's enough! Stop!

1716
02:20:43,330 --> 02:20:45,470
Don't regenerate!

1717
02:20:46,420 --> 02:20:48,459
The fight is over.

1718
02:20:48,460 --> 02:20:50,560
I lost.

1719
02:20:52,210 --> 02:20:55,639
I suffered total defeat
in that moment.

1720
02:20:55,640 --> 02:21:00,060
It was a splendid technique,
fair and honorable.

1721
02:21:01,520 --> 02:21:05,729
He read my movements perfectly,
spun at the last moment,

1722
02:21:05,730 --> 02:21:09,400
and slashed before
I could launch my attack.

1723
02:21:10,190 --> 02:21:12,030
It's over.

1724
02:21:12,860 --> 02:21:17,160
I want to go to Hell gracefully.

1725
02:21:20,160 --> 02:21:22,290
Where does he want to go?

1726
02:21:30,130 --> 02:21:31,750
He stopped.

1727
02:21:34,590 --> 02:21:36,260
Father.

1728
02:21:37,760 --> 02:21:39,550
Are you fine now?

1729
02:21:40,220 --> 02:21:42,010
Are you not suffering now?

1730
02:21:43,390 --> 02:21:45,940
I'm fine, Hakuji.

1731
02:21:46,940 --> 02:21:48,810
Thank you.

1732
02:21:55,190 --> 02:21:57,030
I'm sorry, Father.

1733
02:21:57,530 --> 02:22:01,079
Sorry, I couldn't start over.

1734
02:22:01,080 --> 02:22:02,620
I failed.

1735
02:22:05,830 --> 02:22:07,750
That doesn't matter.

1736
02:22:08,370 --> 02:22:10,719
Whatever you become...

1737
02:22:10,720 --> 02:22:12,209
A son is a son.

1738
02:22:12,210 --> 02:22:14,159
A disciple is a disciple.

1739
02:22:14,160 --> 02:22:16,420
Even in death, we wouldn't abandon you.

1740
02:22:17,880 --> 02:22:21,470
But we can't take you to Heaven.

1741
02:22:23,760 --> 02:22:25,350
Master...

1742
02:22:27,980 --> 02:22:31,979
Didn't you want to become strong?

1743
02:22:31,980 --> 02:22:35,219
Is this the end for you?

1744
02:22:35,220 --> 02:22:37,030
Akaza.

1745
02:22:38,780 --> 02:22:42,449
That's right.
I'm going to be strong.

1746
02:22:42,450 --> 02:22:44,340
I want to be strong.

1747
02:22:45,370 --> 02:22:47,579
So what if he severed my head?

1748
02:22:47,580 --> 02:22:48,829
The fight is over?

1749
02:22:48,830 --> 02:22:50,769
Doesn't matter!

1750
02:22:50,770 --> 02:22:53,500
I'll murder them all.

1751
02:22:54,170 --> 02:22:57,050
I can still get stronger.

1752
02:22:59,630 --> 02:23:03,260
I must fulfill my promise.

1753
02:23:13,560 --> 02:23:17,500
Hakuji, thank you.

1754
02:23:18,190 --> 02:23:20,150
You've done enough.

1755
02:23:24,530 --> 02:23:26,000
It's fine.

1756
02:23:26,670 --> 02:23:28,329
You can stop.

1757
02:23:28,330 --> 02:23:29,960
Akaza!

1758
02:23:39,920 --> 02:23:41,429
Sorry!

1759
02:23:41,430 --> 02:23:44,759
I'm sorry I couldn't protect you!

1760
02:23:44,760 --> 02:23:48,020
I'm sorry I wasn't by your side
when you needed me!

1761
02:23:48,640 --> 02:23:51,559
I couldn't keep a single promise!

1762
02:23:51,560 --> 02:23:53,099
Forgive me!

1763
02:23:53,100 --> 02:23:55,710
Please forgive me!

1764
02:23:56,270 --> 02:23:58,240
Forgive me...

1765
02:24:02,200 --> 02:24:07,120
I'm glad you remembered us.

1766
02:24:08,080 --> 02:24:12,670
I'm glad you returned
to the old Hakuji.

1767
02:24:21,380 --> 02:24:24,680
Welcome back, Hakuji.

1768
02:24:28,560 --> 02:24:30,350
Yo, Hakuji.

1769
02:24:30,800 --> 02:24:32,180
Welcome back.

1770
02:24:40,730 --> 02:24:42,280
I'm back.

1771
02:24:43,240 --> 02:24:44,910
I've finally returned.

1772
02:24:48,580 --> 02:24:52,750
Welcome back, my love.

1773
02:25:21,900 --> 02:25:23,570
He disappeared.

1774
02:25:35,120 --> 02:25:37,630
It's over.

1775
02:25:41,300 --> 02:25:42,800
Hurry...

1776
02:25:43,420 --> 02:25:49,760
I need to go... to Miss Tamayo...

1777
02:25:57,100 --> 02:25:58,650
Tanjiro...

1778
02:26:11,200 --> 02:26:16,499
Tanjiro and Giyu have defeated
Upper Rank Three!

1779
02:26:16,500 --> 02:26:22,000
They lost consciousness
due to extreme exhaustion!

1780
02:26:27,090 --> 02:26:32,679
Tanjiro and Giyu have defeated
Upper Rank Three!

1781
02:26:32,680 --> 02:26:34,100
They have won!

1782
02:26:41,110 --> 02:26:45,690
Akaza's presence is gone.

1783
02:26:48,150 --> 02:26:50,490
He has fallen.

1784
02:26:53,660 --> 02:26:55,200
Akaza.

1785
02:26:56,620 --> 02:27:00,420
Weren't you going to defeat me?

1786
02:27:02,710 --> 02:27:07,050
A path had opened for him
to reach greater heights,

1787
02:27:08,500 --> 02:27:11,930
but he abandoned it himself.

1788
02:27:18,770 --> 02:27:21,730
How utterly weak.

1789
02:27:29,070 --> 02:27:30,609
Oh my?

1790
02:27:30,610 --> 02:27:34,950
Could Sir Akaza be dead?

1791
02:27:36,330 --> 02:27:40,930
I felt a strange sensation for a moment,
but it was probably my imagination.

1792
02:27:41,870 --> 02:27:46,560
As if Sir Akaza had become
a different creature.

1793
02:27:49,420 --> 02:27:52,010
But he's dead now,
I guess I'll never know.

1794
02:27:55,140 --> 02:27:58,140
Okay, what was it?

1795
02:27:59,020 --> 02:28:01,020
Oh, I remember.

1796
02:28:01,520 --> 02:28:03,940
I asked you your name.

1797
02:28:16,800 --> 02:28:22,369
Tanjiro and Giyu have defeated
Upper Rank Three!

1798
02:28:22,370 --> 02:28:23,580
They have won!

1799
02:28:24,290 --> 02:28:25,580
Himejima!

1800
02:28:26,960 --> 02:28:28,880
Well done, Tomioka.

1801
02:28:29,510 --> 02:28:31,420
Well done, Kamado.

1802
02:28:36,640 --> 02:28:40,349
Tomioka and Tanjiro are amazing!

1803
02:28:40,350 --> 02:28:43,040
Now it's our turn!

1804
02:28:43,480 --> 02:28:44,850
Yeah!

1805
02:28:59,540 --> 02:29:01,660
Don't die on us, Agatsuma!

1806
02:29:07,080 --> 02:29:09,549
Hurry or I'll poke you!

1807
02:29:09,550 --> 02:29:10,709
Hear me?

1808
02:29:10,710 --> 02:29:14,679
Show the way to the strongest demon!

1809
02:29:14,680 --> 02:29:16,469
Got it?

1810
02:29:16,470 --> 02:29:18,889
Pig assault!

1811
02:29:18,890 --> 02:29:20,179
Heyah!

1812
02:29:20,180 --> 02:29:21,679
This way!

1813
02:29:21,680 --> 02:29:25,100
We got a tough one over here!

1814
02:29:31,400 --> 02:29:33,440
Where's Big Bro?

1815
02:29:43,340 --> 02:29:45,369
Bring me an Upper Rank!

1816
02:29:45,370 --> 02:29:46,749
Upper Rank!

1817
02:29:46,750 --> 02:29:48,369
Damn it!

1818
02:29:48,370 --> 02:29:51,000
Don't you run away!

1819
02:29:58,890 --> 02:30:04,060
Northern access route from the 88th layer,
Muzan is not found.

1820
02:30:05,230 --> 02:30:09,730
Southeast, 127th layer,
Muzan is not found.

1821
02:30:10,960 --> 02:30:13,649
Where is he? Where is he?

1822
02:30:13,650 --> 02:30:14,820
Where could he be?

1823
02:30:15,690 --> 02:30:20,160
The 90th layer through the 100th layer,
Muzan is not found.

1824
02:30:22,410 --> 02:30:25,289
The 133rd layer, cleared.

1825
02:30:25,290 --> 02:30:27,000
Muzan is not found.

1826
02:30:28,330 --> 02:30:33,340
Our crows will definitely find you.

1827
02:30:33,810 --> 02:30:37,049
We'll search every inch of this castle

1828
02:30:37,050 --> 02:30:41,010
and hunt you down,
no matter where you are.

1829
02:30:56,370 --> 02:30:59,259
Multi-layered structure
moving to the northeast.

1830
02:30:59,260 --> 02:31:03,119
New structures are moving
vertically and horizontally,

1831
02:31:03,120 --> 02:31:04,910
layering over one another...

1832
02:31:08,910 --> 02:31:10,620
...and merging into one!

1833
02:31:17,170 --> 02:31:18,920
It's too much...

1834
02:31:20,130 --> 02:31:21,589
No.

1835
02:31:21,590 --> 02:31:24,670
We can't afford to lose here.

1836
02:31:25,390 --> 02:31:27,599
Crows, go!

1837
02:31:27,600 --> 02:31:29,520
To Muzan!

1838
02:31:34,380 --> 02:31:37,319
You demon hunters are an eyesore!

1839
02:31:37,320 --> 02:31:41,679
You will never reach me.

1840
02:31:41,680 --> 02:31:45,829
You may be feeling proud after
taking the head of an Upper Rank,

1841
02:31:45,830 --> 02:31:50,000
but unless you kill me,
it means nothing.

1842
02:31:53,630 --> 02:31:59,629
You'll die meaninglessly
without ever laying eyes on me.

1843
02:31:59,630 --> 02:32:03,140
Such a fate is fitting for fools like you.

1844
02:32:04,220 --> 02:32:09,310
From this point on,
I'll make you regret being alive.

1845
02:32:10,810 --> 02:32:14,729
Writhe in agony, suffer,
and squirm in despair.

1846
02:32:14,730 --> 02:32:20,189
And this night, demon hunters...

1847
02:32:20,190 --> 02:32:22,610
will be your last!

1848
02:32:33,550 --> 02:32:35,250
Don't die.

1849
02:32:38,840 --> 02:32:40,920
Giyu.

1850
02:32:47,760 --> 02:32:51,350
Don't die on me, Tanjiro.